ailers.</strong></p>\",\"short_description\":\"\",\"location\":\"JW3 Cinema\",\"venue\":{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785204\",\"name\":\"JW3 Cinema\",\"short_name\":\"JW3 Cinema\",\"description\":\"For all booking enquiries, please call the UK Jewish Film box office: 020 3176 0048.\",\"address\":\"341-351 Finchley Road \\nLondon \\nNW3 6ET\",\"default_capacity\":null,\"color\":\"#ff6b94\",\"use_reserved_seating\":true,\"comscore_include\":false,\"seatmap_id\":\"9b66676b-bdd5-0983-1fcb-f293379a36cd\",\"seatmap_categories\":[{\"key\":\"1\",\"label\":\"Adult Standard\",\"color\":\"#992C4E\",\"_id\":\"6ab262e9d7f848654e9c8e14\"},{\"key\":\"2\",\"label\":\"Wheelchair Space (Call UKJF to book)\",\"color\":\"#4176A5\",\"_id\":\"6ab262e9d7f848654e9c8e15\"},{\"key\":\"3\",\"label\":\"Companion Seat (Call UKJF to book)\",\"color\":\"#49A3BA\",\"_id\":\"6ab262e9d7f848654e9c8e16\"},{\"key\":\"4\",\"label\":\"Set Aside\",\"color\":\"#878787\",\"_id\":\"6ab262e9d7f848654e9c8e17\"},{\"key\":\"5\",\"label\":\"House Seats\",\"color\":\"#5d5d5d\",\"_id\":\"6ab262e9d7f848654e9c8e18\"}]},\"is_dated\":true,\"start_time\":\"2026-11-15T16:30:00.000Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-11-15T18:30:00.000Z\",\"cutoff_event_watch_at_availability_end\":false,\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"6aa94c525bba412e1e2417d2\",\"name\":\"+ Pre-Feature Short\",\"color\":\"#3697ff\",\"visible\":true}],\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"hide_tickets_button\":false,\"require_mailing_address\":false,\"require_phone_number\":false,\"rush_line_enabled\":false,\"passholder_ticket_required\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_enabled\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_unlocked\":false,\"sales_disabled_unless_coupon\":false,\"show_custom_checkout_message\":false,\"disable_pass_quick_order\":false,\"credits_disabled\":false,\"tickets_available\":true,\"unlimited\":true,\"quantity\":0,\"ticket_buckets\":[{\"id\":\"6a998bd434a6ff2e068ef0ac\",\"name\":\"Adult Standard\",\"price\":1700,\"unlimited\":true,\"quantity_sold\":13,\"quantity_scanned\":0,\"quantity_remaining\":9007199254740991,\"reserved_seating_category\":\"1\",\"public\":true,\"autoissue_companion_ticket\":[],\"exclude_capacity\":false,\"lock_admin_only\":false,\"variable_price\":false,\"variable_price_minimum\":0,\"variants\":[],\"applicable_pass_buckets\":[],\"is_active\":true,\"virtual_intervals\":null},{\"id\":\"6a998bd434a6ff2e068ef0b3\",\"name\":\"Under 35s (with valid ID)\",\"price\":1000,\"unlimited\":true,\"quantity_sold\":0,\"quantity_scanned\":0,\"quantity_remaining\":9007199254740991,\"reserved_seating_category\":\"1\",\"public\":true,\"autoissue_companion_ticket\":[],\"exclude_capacity\":false,\"lock_admin_only\":false,\"variable_price\":false,\"variable_price_minimum\":0,\"variants\":[],\"applicable_pass_buckets\":[],\"is_active\":true,\"virtual_intervals\":null}],\"films\":[{\"id\":\"6a91ad0c20625c9624c04b7c\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc47850df\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"UK Jewish Film Festival 2026\",\"owner_id\":\"5eabd86394261c0075794000\",\"name\":\"Cancelled\",\"sort_key\":\"Cancelled\",\"description\":\"<p>A truly shocking and timely documentary exposing the horrific rise in violent antisemitism in Australia since the October 7th attacks, particularly in the arts sector. Featuring interviews with Jewish-Australian artists who’ve found themselves cancelled, abused, and attacked as a direct result of their Jewish identities, the film offers a prescient warning about the consequences of letting such anti-Jewish hatred fester. Towards the end of filming, the 2025 Bondi Beach attacks took place in Sydney. In total,15 people, including 13 Jews, were shot and killed by terrorists during a public Chanukah event. The UK premiere of a harrowing but vitally important film.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1788432764961temp-1788432764761-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1788432765495temp-1788432765132-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1788432764537temp-1788432764173-still.jpg\",\"trailer_url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YwCWeX-PIWI\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2026\",\"runtime\":\"85\",\"language\":\"English\",\"country\":\"Australia\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Danny Ben-Moshe\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785275\",\"name\":\"Cinema Screening\",\"color\":\"#36e2ff\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a91ad0c20625c9624c04b78\",\"name\":\"Resilience Strand\",\"color\":\"#ffbc57\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc478527e\",\"name\":\"Feature Film\",\"color\":\"#c78fff\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785272\",\"name\":\"Documentary\",\"color\":\"#8186d0\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785276\",\"name\":\"UK Premiere\",\"color\":\"#9df210\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785274\",\"name\":\"English Language\",\"color\":\"#7ac1f4\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785270\",\"name\":\"Browse All Films\",\"color\":\"#51b4a1\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-28T15:45:16.781Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-15T14:21:06.950Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true},{\"id\":\"6a9e9666b286673ebb9247fc\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc47850df\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"UK Jewish Film Festival 2026\",\"owner_id\":\"5eabd86394261c0075794000\",\"name\":\"Liorah\",\"sort_key\":\"Liorah\",\"description\":\"<p>Poetic and rhythmic, <em>Liorah</em> portrays rising art-world star, Liorah Tchiprout. She draws from her Jewish puppet-dolls to create haunting scenes suspended in time.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1757340175180bc9a4b2371bc6edd01a2.jpg?fit=crop&w=960&h=380\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/17576033720990cf8a06787063fb902ac.jpg?w=300\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1757340184951d9df5ba89e67f50cc761.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"country\":\"United Kingdom\",\"genre\":\"Short, Documentary\",\"language\":\"English\",\"runtime\":\"5\",\"year\":\"2025\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Marcos Wolodarsky, Michelle Wolodarsky\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785270\",\"name\":\"Browse All Films\",\"color\":\"#51b4a1\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785271\",\"name\":\"Short Film\",\"color\":\"#cef2ec\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785272\",\"name\":\"Documentary\",\"color\":\"#8186d0\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785273\",\"name\":\"Dangoor Short Doc Fund\",\"color\":\"#79b1f7\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785274\",\"name\":\"English Language\",\"color\":\"#7ac1f4\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785275\",\"name\":\"Cinema Screening\",\"color\":\"#36e2ff\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785276\",\"name\":\"UK Premiere\",\"color\":\"#9df210\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"virtual_content\":{\"id\":\"6979fd8ce283ad7b05afcc59\",\"type\":\"vod\",\"label\":\"Liorah mp4.mp4\",\"status\":\"ready\",\"status_percent\":100,\"ev_next_encoding_id\":\"6af7d064-7f27-4a41-ad0e-ae71bbc0859f\",\"live_chat_visible\":true,\"live_chat_participation_enabled\":true,\"live_chat_show_viewer_count\":true,\"ams_drm_enabled\":true,\"duration\":312459,\"file_size\":71072487,\"created_at\":\"2026-01-28T12:14:04.602Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-01-28T12:40:23.721Z\",\"platform\":\"ev_next\",\"caption_tracks\":[{\"title\":\"English\",\"url\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/eventive-static/b08e52d60d87773bb2930a5e42c61589.vtt\"}]},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-07T10:48:06.817Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-07T10:48:06.844Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true}],\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-09T10:47:51.529Z\",\"is_virtual\":false,\"comscore_include\":true,\"geographic_restrictions\":[],\"geographic_exclusions\":[],\"vague_geographic_restrictions\":false,\"show_in_coming_soon\":false,\"allow_preorder\":false,\"aarp_member_required\":false,\"show_quantity_countdown\":false,\"virtual_balloting_enabled\":false,\"virtual_balloting_inline_during_playback\":false,\"use_default_event_bucket_preroll\":true,\"virtual_content_preroll\":[],\"virtual_content_preroll_visible\":true,\"use_default_event_bucket_postroll\":true,\"virtual_content_postroll\":[],\"virtual_content_postroll_visible\":true,\"virtual_intervals\":null,\"display_ads\":[],\"images\":{},\"ledger_tags\":[],\"rules\":[]},{\"id\":\"6a9708ea415f2c5e1404d930\",\"event_bucket\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc47850df\",\"timezone\":\"Europe/London\",\"name\":\"CLOSING NIGHT GALA: The Last Concert\",\"description\":\"<h1>CLOSING NIGHT GALA</h1><h3>+ Q&amp;A with director Alexandre Arcady</h3><p><strong>PRICES:</strong></p><p><strong>Adult Standard: £30.00</strong></p><p><br></p><p>Tickets for this event are sold directly through Curzon Cinemas. Clicking the \\\"Order Tickets\\\" button will take you to their booking website.</p><p>There is a £2.00 booking fee for all bookings made via the Curzon website.</p><p><br></p><p>For all enquiries relating to your booking, please contact Curzon directly.</p><p>Curzon Ticket Booking Line: 08719 642838 (Calls to the ticket booking line cost 13p per minute, plus your service provider fees. Please be aware that there is a £2 booking fee for phone bookings.)</p><p>Curzon Customer Service: 01233 555644 (Local rates service. Please be aware, it is not possible to book tickets via this number.)</p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\\\"background-color: rgb(43, 41, 37); color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\\\">This screening will begin at the advertised time with no ads or trailers.</strong></p><p><br></p><h4>Sponsored by:</h4><h4>Isabelle and Ivor Seddon</h4><p><br></p><p><img src=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/eventive-static/f1fa628af503a71ec0c1d1b0a65713d8.png\\\" width=\\\"178\\\"></p>\",\"short_description\":\"\",\"location\":\"Curzon Mayfair\",\"venue\":{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc478520c\",\"name\":\"Curzon Mayfair\",\"short_name\":\"Curzon Mayfair\",\"description\":\"For all booking enquiries, please call the venue directly: 08719 642838\",\"address\":\"Curzon Mayfair\\n38 Curzon St\\nLondon W1J 7TY\",\"default_capacity\":null,\"color\":\"#608ea4\",\"use_reserved_seating\":true,\"comscore_include\":false,\"seatmap_id\":\"cd261459-295f-302d-71e8-8c70ad0ba790\",\"seatmap_categories\":[{\"key\":\"1\",\"label\":\"Adult Standard\",\"color\":\"#992C4E\",\"_id\":\"675c5c67a9d65c62d8dea834\"},{\"key\":\"2\",\"label\":\"Wheelchair Space (Call box office to book)\",\"color\":\"#4176A5\",\"_id\":\"675c5c67a9d65c62d8dea835\"},{\"key\":\"3\",\"label\":\"Guests\",\"color\":\"#d3d3d3\",\"_id\":\"675c5c67a9d65c62d8dea836\"},{\"key\":\"4\",\"label\":\"Companion Seat (Call box office to book)\",\"color\":\"#49A3BA\",\"_id\":\"675c5c67a9d65c62d8dea837\"}]},\"is_dated\":true,\"start_time\":\"2026-11-15T17:30:00.000Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-11-15T19:30:00.000Z\",\"cutoff_event_watch_at_availability_end\":false,\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"6aa94c3d49d98ac93d6e069f\",\"name\":\"+ Q&A\",\"color\":\"#7fff36\",\"visible\":true}],\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"hide_tickets_button\":false,\"require_mailing_address\":false,\"require_phone_number\":false,\"rush_line_enabled\":false,\"passholder_ticket_required\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_enabled\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_unlocked\":false,\"sales_disabled_unless_coupon\":false,\"show_custom_checkout_message\":false,\"external_tickets_url\":\"https://www.curzon.com/ticketing/seats/MAY1-34615/\",\"disable_pass_quick_order\":false,\"credits_disabled\":true,\"tickets_available\":true,\"unlimited\":false,\"quantity\":0,\"ticket_buckets\":[],\"films\":[{\"id\":\"6a8f21f1577ecc984c485fa4\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc47850df\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"UK Jewish Film Festival 2026\",\"owner_id\":\"5eabd86394261c0075794000\",\"name\":\"The Last Concert\",\"sort_key\":\"Last Concert, The\",\"description\":\"<p>A thrilling cat-and-mouse psychological drama from legendary director, Alexandre Arcady, who won Best Film at the 2024 UK Jewish Film Festival with Once Upon a Time in Algeria. Renowned but tyrannical classical composer, Alexandre Miller (Benoît Poelvoorde), performs a farewell concert at the iconic Opéra-Comique in Paris, before he leaves to take over the Berlin Philharmonic. After the performance, a man named Dinkel (Kad Merad) arrives. He claims to be a super-fan of Miller, and insists on a private audience with his hero. As Dinkel relentlessly pursues Miller through the labyrinthine corridors of the opera house, dark secrets from their past begin to emerge.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1787931964715temp-1787931964612-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1787931963742temp-1787931963464-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1787765544906temp-1787765544380-still.jpg\",\"trailer_url\":\"https://youtu.be/v-1Ue9codho\",\"unballoted\":true,\"details\":{\"country\":\"Belgium, France\",\"language\":\"French\",\"runtime\":\"89\",\"subtitle_language\":\"English\",\"year\":\"2026\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Alexandre Arcady\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"6a91ad0c20625c9624c04b23\",\"name\":\"French Language\",\"color\":\"#8d95ff\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc478527c\",\"name\":\"Drama\",\"color\":\"#f9b6df\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a91ad0c20625c9624c04b0d\",\"name\":\"English Subtitles\",\"color\":\"#3697ff\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785276\",\"name\":\"UK Premiere\",\"color\":\"#9df210\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc478527f\",\"name\":\"Comedy\",\"color\":\"#ffdeee\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a91ad0c20625c9624c04b32\",\"name\":\"Comedy Drama\",\"color\":\"#3697ff\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785281\",\"name\":\"Gala Film\",\"color\":\"#ffc636\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a91ad0c20625c9624c04b40\",\"name\":\"Closing Night Gala\",\"color\":\"#608ea4\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785270\",\"name\":\"Browse All Films\",\"color\":\"#51b4a1\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc478527e\",\"name\":\"Feature Film\",\"color\":\"#c78fff\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785275\",\"name\":\"Cinema Screening\",\"color\":\"#36e2ff\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-26T17:27:13.243Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-14T15:25:22.381Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true}],\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-09T10:48:01.824Z\",\"is_virtual\":false,\"comscore_include\":true,\"geographic_restrictions\":[],\"geographic_exclusions\":[],\"vague_geographic_restrictions\":false,\"show_in_coming_soon\":false,\"allow_preorder\":false,\"aarp_member_required\":false,\"show_quantity_countdown\":false,\"virtual_balloting_enabled\":false,\"virtual_balloting_inline_during_playback\":false,\"use_default_event_bucket_preroll\":true,\"virtual_content_preroll\":[],\"virtual_content_preroll_visible\":true,\"use_default_event_bucket_postroll\":true,\"virtual_content_postroll\":[],\"virtual_content_postroll_visible\":true,\"virtual_intervals\":null,\"display_ads\":[],\"images\":{},\"ledger_tags\":[],\"rules\":[]},{\"id\":\"6ac3c644d1e34c35110d3162\",\"event_bucket\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc47850df\",\"timezone\":\"Europe/London\",\"name\":\"The Soundman\",\"description\":\"<h6>\\\"This film is a standout: meditative, innovative, and profoundly moving.\\\"&nbsp;</h6><h3><em>The Hollywood Times</em></h3><h6>\\\"The Soundman is a film like an opera, where music, play and image come together in optimal synergy\\\"</h6><h3><em>Cinemagazine</em></h3><h6>“The Soundman is a poetic declaration of love to the world of sound and at the same time a moving historical drama”</h6><h3><em>Moviebreak</em></h3><p><br></p><h4>This film will be shown in Screen 2</h4><p><strong>PRICES:</strong></p><p><strong>Standard Seat: £12.00</strong></p><p><strong>Seniors (60+) / Blue Light: £10.00</strong></p><p><strong>Students (with valid ID): £9.00</strong></p><p><strong>Disabled, Unwaged: £8.00</strong></p><p><strong>Under 18s: £7.00</strong></p><p><br></p><p>Tickets for this event are sold directly through Broadway Cinema, Nottingham. Clicking the \\\"Order Tickets\\\" will take you to their booking website.</p><p>All orders placed with Broadway Cinema will be subject to a fee of £1.50.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>For all enquiries relating to your booking, please contact Broadway Cinema directly.</p><p>Box Office: 0115 952 6611 (Open daily from 12.00pm)</p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\\\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: rgb(43, 41, 37);\\\">This screening will begin at the advertised time with no ads or trailers.</strong></p>\",\"short_description\":\"\",\"location\":\"Nottingham Broadway\",\"venue\":{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc47851ee\",\"name\":\"Nottingham Broadway\",\"short_name\":\"Nottingham Broadway\",\"description\":\"For all booking enquiries, please call the venue directly: 0115 952 6611\",\"address\":\"Nottingham Broadway\\n14-18 Broad St\\nNottingham NG1 3AL\",\"default_capacity\":null,\"color\":\"#7fff36\",\"use_reserved_seating\":true,\"comscore_include\":false,\"seatmap_categories\":[]},\"is_dated\":true,\"start_time\":\"2026-11-15T17:30:00.000Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-11-15T19:30:00.000Z\",\"cutoff_event_watch_at_availability_end\":false,\"tags\":[],\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"hide_tickets_button\":false,\"require_mailing_address\":false,\"require_phone_number\":false,\"rush_line_enabled\":false,\"passholder_ticket_required\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_enabled\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_unlocked\":false,\"sales_disabled_unless_coupon\":false,\"show_custom_checkout_message\":false,\"external_tickets_url\":\"https://broadway.org.uk/book/1238801\",\"disable_pass_quick_order\":false,\"credits_disabled\":true,\"tickets_available\":true,\"unlimited\":false,\"quantity\":0,\"ticket_buckets\":[],\"films\":[{\"id\":\"6a91ad0c20625c9624c04b4d\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc47850df\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"UK Jewish Film Festival 2026\",\"owner_id\":\"5eabd86394261c0075794000\",\"name\":\"The Soundman\",\"sort_key\":\"Soundman, The\",\"description\":\"<p>A beautiful portrayal of young love swept up by the dark tides of history, and a remarkable cinematic depiction of sound. In May 1940, German forces are massing along the borders of Belgium, Luxembourg, and the Netherlands. At a Brussels radio station, Elza (Femke Vanhove) is a talented young voice actor. She’s also, secretly, a Jewish refugee from Vienna. Meanwhile, Berre (Jef Hellemans) is an innovative introverted sound engineer, who creates the sound effects for the station's radio plays. The two fall deeply in love, but as war looms, and Elza’s true identity is exposed, their relationship is put to the ultimate test.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1791287981705temp-1791287981644-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1791287989805temp-1791287989748-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1791287989517temp-1791287989461-still.jpg\",\"trailer_url\":\"https://youtu.be/cmLvljVT4pY?si=DMJa4OoocUQVXSSI\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2025\",\"runtime\":\"120\",\"language\":\"Dutch, Hebrew\",\"country\":\"Belgium\",\"subtitle_language\":\"English\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Frank Van Passel\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785275\",\"name\":\"Cinema Screening\",\"color\":\"#36e2ff\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a91ad0c20625c9624c04b4e\",\"name\":\"Memory Strand\",\"color\":\"#ffbc57\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc478527c\",\"name\":\"Drama\",\"color\":\"#f9b6df\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a91ad0c20625c9624c04b4f\",\"name\":\"Historical Drama\",\"color\":\"#cef2ec\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785276\",\"name\":\"UK Premiere\",\"color\":\"#9df210\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a91ad0c20625c9624c04b50\",\"name\":\"Dutch Language\",\"color\":\"#ff8fdc\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a91ad0c20625c9624c04b11\",\"name\":\"Hebrew Language\",\"color\":\"#8d95ff\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a91ad0c20625c9624c04b0d\",\"name\":\"English Subtitles\",\"color\":\"#3697ff\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc478527e\",\"name\":\"Feature Film\",\"color\":\"#c78fff\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785270\",\"name\":\"Browse All Films\",\"color\":\"#51b4a1\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-28T15:45:16.702Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-08T14:10:22.745Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true}],\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-13T11:32:10.897Z\",\"is_virtual\":false,\"comscore_include\":true,\"geographic_restrictions\":[],\"geographic_exclusions\":[],\"vague_geographic_restrictions\":false,\"show_in_coming_soon\":false,\"allow_preorder\":false,\"aarp_member_required\":false,\"show_quantity_countdown\":false,\"virtual_balloting_enabled\":false,\"virtual_balloting_inline_during_playback\":false,\"use_default_event_bucket_preroll\":true,\"virtual_content_preroll\":[],\"virtual_content_preroll_visible\":true,\"use_default_event_bucket_postroll\":true,\"virtual_content_postroll\":[],\"virtual_content_postroll_visible\":true,\"virtual_intervals\":null,\"display_ads\":[],\"images\":{},\"ledger_tags\":[],\"rules\":[]},{\"id\":\"6a9708ea415f2c5e1404d941\",\"event_bucket\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc47850df\",\"timezone\":\"Europe/London\",\"name\":\"DOC DAY: Noga\",\"description\":\"<h2>PART OF DOC DAY AT CURZON BLOOMSBURY</h2><h4>This film will be shown in Screen 5 (The Renoir)</h4><p><strong>PRICES:</strong></p><p><strong>Adult Standard: £20.00</strong></p><p><br></p><p>Tickets for this event are sold directly through Curzon Cinemas. Clicking the \\\"Order Tickets\\\" button will take you to their booking website.</p><p>There is a £2.00 booking fee for all bookings made via the Curzon website.</p><p><br></p><p>For all enquiries relating to your booking, please contact Curzon directly.</p><p>Curzon Ticket Booking Line: 08719 642838 (Calls to the ticket booking line cost 13p per minute, plus your service provider fees. Please be aware that there is a £2 booking fee for phone bookings.)</p><p>Curzon Customer Service: 01233 555644 (Local rates service. Please be aware, it is not possible to book tickets via this number.)</p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\\\"background-color: rgb(43, 41, 37); color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\\\">This screening will begin at the advertised time with no ads or trailers.</strong></p>\",\"short_description\":\"\",\"location\":\"Curzon Bloomsbury\",\"venue\":{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc47851ea\",\"name\":\"Curzon Bloomsbury\",\"short_name\":\"Curzon Bloomsbury\",\"description\":\"For all booking enquiries, please call the venue directly: 08719 642838.\\nFor Customer Service queries, call: 01233 555644.\",\"address\":\"The Brunswick Centre, London WC1N 1AW\",\"default_capacity\":null,\"color\":\"#8d95ff\",\"use_reserved_seating\":false,\"comscore_include\":false},\"is_dated\":true,\"start_time\":\"2026-11-15T18:30:00.000Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-11-15T20:30:00.000Z\",\"cutoff_event_watch_at_availability_end\":false,\"tags\":[],\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"hide_tickets_button\":false,\"require_mailing_address\":false,\"require_phone_number\":false,\"rush_line_enabled\":false,\"passholder_ticket_required\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_enabled\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_unlocked\":false,\"sales_disabled_unless_coupon\":false,\"show_custom_checkout_message\":false,\"external_tickets_url\":\"https://www.curzon.com/ticketing/seats/BLO1-113623/\",\"disable_pass_quick_order\":false,\"credits_disabled\":true,\"tickets_available\":true,\"unlimited\":false,\"quantity\":0,\"ticket_buckets\":[],\"films\":[{\"id\":\"6a91ad0c20625c9624c04b75\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc47850df\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"UK Jewish Film Festival 2026\",\"owner_id\":\"5eabd86394261c0075794000\",\"name\":\"Noga\",\"sort_key\":\"Noga\",\"description\":\"<p>How does it feel to be a prominent Israeli artist during a time of virulent anti-Israel sentiment? This fly-on-the-wall documentary, about Israeli singer-songwriter, Noga Erez, gives us a first-hand account. Noga is one of Israel’s most successful musical artists. She has performed at major international festivals, including Coachella, and has worked with artists such as Robbie Williams, Missy Elliott, and Florence + The Machine. But after October 7th, and the subsequent war in Gaza, she faced a wave of protests and cancellations. This intimate film ends with Noga offering a heartfelt call for empathy, humanity, and shared understanding, rather than cultural boycotts.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1787932023890temp-1787932023785-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1787932022864temp-1787932022567-poster.jpg\",\"trailer_url\":\"https://youtu.be/s1PKk_RL6wY\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2026\",\"runtime\":\"96\",\"language\":\"Hebrew, English\",\"country\":\"USA, Germany, Israel, Austria\",\"subtitle_language\":\"English\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Benjamin Bergmann, Jono Bergmann\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785275\",\"name\":\"Cinema Screening\",\"color\":\"#36e2ff\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc478527e\",\"name\":\"Feature Film\",\"color\":\"#c78fff\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a91ad0c20625c9624c04b6f\",\"name\":\"Perspectives Strand\",\"color\":\"#3697ff\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785272\",\"name\":\"Documentary\",\"color\":\"#8186d0\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785276\",\"name\":\"UK Premiere\",\"color\":\"#9df210\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a91ad0c20625c9624c04b11\",\"name\":\"Hebrew Language\",\"color\":\"#8d95ff\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785274\",\"name\":\"English Language\",\"color\":\"#7ac1f4\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a91ad0c20625c9624c04b0d\",\"name\":\"English Subtitles\",\"color\":\"#3697ff\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785270\",\"name\":\"Browse All Films\",\"color\":\"#51b4a1\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-28T15:45:16.769Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-03T10:16:22.417Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true}],\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-09T10:48:27.434Z\",\"is_virtual\":false,\"comscore_include\":true,\"geographic_restrictions\":[],\"geographic_exclusions\":[],\"vague_geographic_restrictions\":false,\"show_in_coming_soon\":false,\"allow_preorder\":false,\"aarp_member_required\":false,\"show_quantity_countdown\":false,\"virtual_balloting_enabled\":false,\"virtual_balloting_inline_during_playback\":false,\"use_default_event_bucket_preroll\":true,\"virtual_content_preroll\":[],\"virtual_content_preroll_visible\":true,\"use_default_event_bucket_postroll\":true,\"virtual_content_postroll\":[],\"virtual_content_postroll_visible\":true,\"virtual_intervals\":null,\"display_ads\":[],\"images\":{},\"ledger_tags\":[],\"rules\":[]},{\"id\":\"6aa80388d60d7c117dcc4ad8\",\"event_bucket\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc47850df\",\"timezone\":\"Europe/London\",\"name\":\"British-Jewish Life on Film: Norwich\",\"description\":\"<h4>This film will be shown in Screen 2</h4><p><strong>PRICES:</strong></p><p><strong>Adult Standard: £14.50</strong></p><p><strong>Students / Over 60s (with valid ID): £10.99</strong></p><p><strong>Universal Credit (with valid ID): £6.99</strong></p><p><br></p><p>Tickets for this event are sold directly through Picturehouse Cinemas. Clicking the \\\"Order Tickets\\\" button will take you to their booking website. If you already have an account with Picturehouse Cinemas, you can either log in, or click \\\"Continue as Guest\\\" to proceed.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>For all enquiries relating to your booking, please contact Picturehouse directly.</p><p>Picturehouse Customer Service: 0207 326 2649 (Phone lines are open Monday to Sunday, 10am to 6pm)</p><p>Picturehouse Ticket Booking Line: 0871 902 5747 (Calls to the ticket booking line cost 13p per minute, plus your service provider fees.)</p><p><br></p><p>We are proud to present <em>British Jewish Life on Film 2026: </em>an evening of brand new films about British Jewish life. These films were all commissioned this year by UKJF's Film Factory, with the aim of demonstrating the absolute diversity of our community. A series of mini-documentaries and short dramas tell Jewish stories from the length and breadth of the UK.</p><p><br></p><p>You'll laugh, you'll cry, you'll be entertained, you'll discover things you didn't know, and just by turning up to the screening you'll meet other local members of the Jewish community.</p><p><br></p><p>Above all else, you're guaranteed to leave feeling a renewed sense of Jewish pride.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\\\"background-color: rgb(43, 41, 37); color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\\\">This screening will begin at the advertised time with no ads or trailers.</strong></p>\",\"short_description\":\"\",\"location\":\"Cinema City Norwich\",\"venue\":{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc478521d\",\"name\":\"Cinema City Norwich\",\"short_name\":\"Cinema City\",\"description\":\"For all booking enquiries, please call the venue directly: 0871 902 5747\",\"address\":\"St Andrews St\\nNorwich \\nNR2 4AD\",\"default_capacity\":null,\"color\":\"#608ea4\",\"use_reserved_seating\":false,\"comscore_include\":false},\"is_dated\":true,\"start_time\":\"2026-11-17T18:15:00.000Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-11-17T20:15:00.000Z\",\"cutoff_event_watch_at_availability_end\":false,\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"6aa7f91cd5377103a57d3460\",\"name\":\"British Jewish Life on Film\",\"color\":\"#ff8fdc\",\"visible\":true}],\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"hide_tickets_button\":false,\"require_mailing_address\":false,\"require_phone_number\":false,\"rush_line_enabled\":false,\"passholder_ticket_required\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_enabled\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_unlocked\":false,\"sales_disabled_unless_coupon\":false,\"show_custom_checkout_message\":false,\"external_tickets_url\":\"https://web.picturehouses.com/order/showtimes/001-65364/seats\",\"disable_pass_quick_order\":false,\"credits_disabled\":true,\"tickets_available\":true,\"unlimited\":false,\"quantity\":0,\"ticket_buckets\":[],\"films\":[{\"id\":\"6a91ad0c20625c9624c04afc\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc47850df\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"UK Jewish Film Festival 2026\",\"owner_id\":\"5eabd86394261c0075794000\",\"name\":\"King of the Jews\",\"sort_key\":\"King of the Jews\",\"description\":\"<p>When Alice and Benj's eight-year-old Jewish son, Ezra, is cast as King Herod in his school Nativity, the couple clash over whether to intervene. The debate escalates as the two argue over who has final say in an interfaith family. Benj, playing the ‘Jewish card’, insists they should stay out of it, scarred by memories of his own overbearing parents, that is, until he sees Ezra's gleefully murderous rehearsal.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1788344937313temp-1788344937283-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1788344937509temp-1788344937488-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1788344937062temp-1788344936948-still.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2026\",\"runtime\":\"7\",\"language\":\"English\",\"country\":\"UK\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Katie Lambert\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc478527d\",\"name\":\"Pears Short Film Fund\",\"color\":\"#ff8fdc\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785271\",\"name\":\"Short Film\",\"color\":\"#cef2ec\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785275\",\"name\":\"Cinema Screening\",\"color\":\"#36e2ff\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785276\",\"name\":\"UK Premiere\",\"color\":\"#9df210\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785274\",\"name\":\"English Language\",\"color\":\"#7ac1f4\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785270\",\"name\":\"Browse All Films\",\"color\":\"#51b4a1\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-28T15:45:16.550Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-02T10:28:56.946Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true},{\"id\":\"6a91ad0c20625c9624c04afe\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc47850df\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"UK Jewish Film Festival 2026\",\"owner_id\":\"5eabd86394261c0075794000\",\"name\":\"Fish, Chips & Faith\",\"sort_key\":\"Fish, Chips & Faith\",\"description\":\"<p>Fish, Chips & Faith tells the uplifting story of a Leeds restaurant bringing communities together by serving Kosher and Halal food under one roof.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1787931926719temp-1787931926616-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1787931925569temp-1787931925377-poster.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2026\",\"runtime\":\"6\",\"language\":\"English\",\"country\":\"UK\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Micaela Blitz, Miriam Rosenberg\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc478526b\",\"name\":\"Dangoor UKJF Short Doc Fund\",\"color\":\"#7fff36\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785271\",\"name\":\"Short Film\",\"color\":\"#cef2ec\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785275\",\"name\":\"Cinema Screening\",\"color\":\"#36e2ff\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785276\",\"name\":\"UK Premiere\",\"color\":\"#9df210\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785274\",\"name\":\"English Language\",\"color\":\"#7ac1f4\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785270\",\"name\":\"Browse All Films\",\"color\":\"#51b4a1\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-28T15:45:16.556Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-09T11:19:34.628Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true},{\"id\":\"6a91ad0c20625c9624c04b06\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc47850df\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"UK Jewish Film Festival 2026\",\"owner_id\":\"5eabd86394261c0075794000\",\"name\":\"Rambling\",\"sort_key\":\"Rambling\",\"description\":\"<p>Over the last 50 years The Pennine Wayfarers have become a community all of their own. Combining friendship and adventure, they travel a route that resonates with British-Jewish history.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1787931934825temp-1787931934741-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1787931933876temp-1787931933813-poster.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2026\",\"runtime\":\"6\",\"language\":\"English\",\"country\":\"UK\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Jack Levy\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc478526b\",\"name\":\"Dangoor UKJF Short Doc Fund\",\"color\":\"#7fff36\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785271\",\"name\":\"Short Film\",\"color\":\"#cef2ec\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785275\",\"name\":\"Cinema Screening\",\"color\":\"#36e2ff\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785276\",\"name\":\"UK Premiere\",\"color\":\"#9df210\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785274\",\"name\":\"English Language\",\"color\":\"#7ac1f4\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785270\",\"name\":\"Browse All Films\",\"color\":\"#51b4a1\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-28T15:45:16.572Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-09T11:18:46.060Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true},{\"id\":\"6a91ad0c20625c9624c04b0b\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"6a300