 her local community. A comment she makes about xenophobia, in a speech given after a terror attack in Rome, however, threatens her privileged, free-spirited existence, and exposes her to the very dark forces she has warned about. Dolce Fine Giornata is an elegant and incisive take on Europe’s refugee crisis, and what has remained of its post-war liberal values. </p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1787931951237temp-1787931951170-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1787931950254temp-1787931950054-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/09a444df120f453e2b8e0f4d707741d8.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"language\":\"Italian, Polish, French\",\"runtime\":\"96\",\"year\":\"2019\",\"country\":\"Poland\",\"subtitle_language\":\"English\"},\"credits\":{\"animator\":null,\"cast\":\"Krystyna Janda, Kasia Smutniak, Vincent Riotta\",\"cinematographer\":null,\"co_producer\":\"Michal Cechnicki\",\"composer\":null,\"director\":\"Jacek Borcuch\",\"editor\":\"Przemysław Chruścielewski\",\"executive_producer\":null,\"filmmaker\":null,\"music\":null,\"producer\":\"Marta Lewandowska, Marta Habior\",\"production_design\":null,\"screenwriter\":\"Jacek Borcuch, Szczepan Twardoch\",\"sound_design\":null},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"6a91ad0c20625c9624c04b2e\",\"name\":\"Best of 30 Strand\",\"color\":\"#fffc36\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc478527e\",\"name\":\"Feature Film\",\"color\":\"#c78fff\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a91ad0c20625c9624c04b14\",\"name\":\"Online\",\"color\":\"#fffc36\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc478527e\",\"name\":\"Feature Film\",\"color\":\"#c78fff\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785270\",\"name\":\"Browse All Films\",\"color\":\"#51b4a1\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc478527c\",\"name\":\"Drama\",\"color\":\"#f9b6df\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a91ad0c20625c9624c04b30\",\"name\":\"Italian Language\",\"color\":\"