ng and old. It’s London, 1960, and 11-year-old David Wiseman is only interested in one thing: cricket. The problem is, he’s not very good at it. When a Jamaican family moves in next door and builds a cricket net in their backyard, David is delighted, but it isn’t long before the neighbourhood is shaken up. With wonderful performances by the entire cast, and an energetic soundtrack of calypso, reggae, and ska recordings, director, Paul Morrison, offers an engrossing look at race relations, racism, and the plight of immigrants in postwar London. </p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1787931959593temp-1787931959576-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1787931958705temp-1787931958697-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/8967214542297b08a223d3cfc327fe77.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"language\":\"English, Hebrew, Yiddish\",\"runtime\":\"106\",\"year\":\"2003\",\"country\":\"UK, Germany\",\"subtitle_language\":\"English\"},\"credits\":{\"animator\":null,\"cast\":\"Sam Smith, Emily Woof, Stanley Townsend\",\"cinematographer\":\"Nina Kellgren\",\"co_producer\":\"Lesley Stewart\",\"composer\":\"Ilona Sekacz\",\"director\":\"Paul Morrison\",\"editor\":\"David Freeman\",\"executive_producer\":\"Kevin Loader, Michael Kuhn\",\"filmmaker\":null,\"music\":null,\"producer\":\"Jonny Persey\",\"production_design\":\"Eve Stewart\",\"screenwriter\":\"Paul Morrison\",\"sound_design\":null},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"6a91ad0c20625c9624c04b2e\",\"name\":\"Best of 30 Strand\",\"color\":\"#fffc36\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc478527e\",\"name\":\"Feature Film\",\"color\":\"#c78fff\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a91ad0c20625c9624c04b14\",\"name\":\"Online\",\"color\":\"#fffc36\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc478527e\",\"name\":\"Feature Film\",\"color\":\"#c78fff\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6a3000f01f63771bc4785270\",\"name\":\"Browse All Films\",\"color\":\"#51b4a1\