          "content": {
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "text": "{\"events\":[{\"id\":\"6aac7f105daf7a756ce1b8a4\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"timezone\":\"Europe/London\",\"name\":\"Indigenous Arctic Cinema & Arts\",\"description\":\"<p><strong>Special guests &amp; display:</strong></p><p><strong>Dennis Inuk Aningaaq Møller</strong> (in-person) – Director, photographer, and poet from Kalaallit Nunaat (Greenland) <a href=\\\"https://tulugaqfilms.com/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">https://tulugaqfilms.com/</a> Supported by Danish Film Institute.</p><p><strong><u>Dr Charlotte Connolly</u></strong> (online) – Head Curator at the <a href=\\\"https://www.scienceandmediamuseum.org.uk/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">National Science and Media Museum</a> (curator of <a href=\\\"https://www.spri.cam.ac.uk/museum/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">The Polar Museum</a> 2015–2022 and current Institute Associate at the <a href=\\\"https://www.spri.cam.ac.uk/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">Scott Polar Research Institute</a>) <a href=\\\"https://charlotteconnelly.com/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">https://charlotteconnelly.com/</a></p><p><strong>On display:</strong> A selection of works by contemporary artists from Iñupiat Nunaat and Yugtun (Alaska), Nunavut, collected by Dr Connolly; moose hide mittens and caribou pelt courtesy of Native Spirit Foundation.</p>\",\"short_description\":\"\",\"location\":\"The Polar Museum\",\"venue\":{\"id\":\"6350b08aa43ea10ff05552cb\",\"name\":\"The Polar Museum\",\"short_name\":\"PolarMuseum\",\"description\":\"The Scott Polar Research Institute is a centre for research into the polar regions and glaciology worldwide. It is a sub-department of the Department of Geography in the University of Cambridge.\",\"address\":\"Lensfield Road Cambridge CB2 1ER\",\"default_capacity\":null,\"color\":\"#d2f3f7\",\"use_reserved_seating\":false,\"comscore_include\":true},\"is_dated\":true,\"start_time\":\"2026-11-03T18:00:00.000Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-11-03T21:00:00.000Z\",\"cutoff_event_watch_at_availability_end\":false,\"tags\":[],\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"hide_tickets_button\":false,\"require_mailing_address\":false,\"require_phone_number\":false,\"rush_line_enabled\":false,\"passholder_ticket_required\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_enabled\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_unlocked\":false,\"sales_disabled_unless_coupon\":false,\"show_custom_checkout_message\":false,\"external_tickets_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/native-spirit-festival-20th-edition-indigenous-arctic-cinema-tickets-2002037414801\",\"disable_pass_quick_order\":false,\"credits_disabled\":true,\"tickets_available\":true,\"unlimited\":false,\"quantity\":0,\"ticket_buckets\":[],\"films\":[{\"id\":\"6aa726811239157d744e426a\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"Deneege Leł Ghu Kk’ots’eedeneeyh Te Heł Hoozoonh Ts’e Denots’edeneeyh\",\"sort_key\":\"Deneege Leł Ghu Kk’ots’eedeneeyh Te Heł Hoozoonh Ts’e Denots’edeneeyh\",\"description\":\"<p>The tradition of tanning hides with brains was once practiced by every Dené person in Alaska. An art that was nearly lost by assimilation, Kathleen Hildebrand works with a group of Dené women at her urban backyard hide camp in the heart of Chen’o (Fairbanks) to revive this tradition.</p><p>One of the few films out there narrated in Denaakk’e, we learn alongside the women how the hides have healing.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789689508014temp-1789689507959-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789689490261temp-1789689490246-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789689500656temp-1789689500616-still.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2026\",\"runtime\":\"5\",\"country\":\"Canada, Finland, Greenland, Norway, United States\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Brittany Woods-Orrison\",\"screenwriter\":\"Brittany Woods-Orrison\",\"producer\":\"Sadetło Scott, Brittany Woods-Orrison\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"62eafd839957df004bd01b7b\",\"name\":\"Short\",\"color\":\"#7fff36\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"62eafd6b54339000d369108b\",\"name\":\"microIndigenous\",\"color\":\"#fffc36\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T22:41:05.518Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T23:59:44.650Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true},{\"id\":\"6aa726811239157d744e4274\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"We are all connected\",\"sort_key\":\"We are all connected\",\"description\":\"<p>A reflection on ancestral spirits and our broken bond with Nature, told through compelling imagery and an Inuit perspective.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789858326530temp-1789858326480-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789858326754temp-1789858326719-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789858326268temp-1789858326129-still.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2025\",\"runtime\":\"4\",\"language\":\"Kalaallisut\",\"country\":\"Greenland\",\"subtitle_language\":\"English\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Arina Kleist\",\"screenwriter\":\"Arina Kleist\",\"producer\":\"Arina Kleist, Princess Daazhraii Johnson\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"62eafd839957df004bd01b7b\",\"name\":\"Short\",\"color\":\"#7fff36\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"62eafd6b54339000d369108b\",\"name\":\"microIndigenous\",\"color\":\"#fffc36\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T22:41:05.527Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-19T22:52:06.126Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true},{\"id\":\"6aa726811239157d744e4236\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"Pinngortitarlu Oqaloqatigiinneq (Dialogue With Nature)\",\"sort_key\":\"Pinngortitarlu Oqaloqatigiinneq (Dialogue With Nature)\",\"short_description\":\"Visual poetry shot on super 8, a call for action on preservation of nature.\",\"description\":\"<p>A sense of nostalgia, a taste of realness in a world of artificiality. </p><p>Sadness and longing being in between worlds, (urban and rural.) </p><p>Constant dialogue inside oneself about loss from the ancient soul, whispering in a modern world.</p><p><br></p><p>Living in this time of the world, out of touch, where slowness feels like a punishment rather than peace and attentive.</p><p><br></p><p>Dreamlike atmosphere, floaty feeling and longing in between, feeling cast away from both worlds and feeling rootless while admiring the beauty of small details.</p><p><br></p><p>A sense of euphoria and a sense of timeless peace, a connection to the ancient world. </p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789859619625temp-1789859619595-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789859690282temp-1789859690273-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789859690058temp-1789859689945-still.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2026\",\"runtime\":\"4\",\"language\":\"Kalaallisut\",\"country\":\"Greenland\",\"facebook\":\"https://www.facebook.com/dennis.k.moller/\",\"instagram\":\"https://www.instagram.com/irondennis/\",\"subtitle_language\":\"English\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Dennis Tulugaq (MÃ¸ller)\",\"screenwriter\":\"Dennis Tulugaq (MÃ¸ller)\",\"producer\":\"Dennis Tulugaq (MÃ¸ller)\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"62eafd839957df004bd01b7b\",\"name\":\"Short\",\"color\":\"#7fff36\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"62eafd6b54339000d369108b\",\"name\":\"microIndigenous\",\"color\":\"#fffc36\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T22:41:05.471Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-19T23:14:49.942Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true},{\"id\":\"6aa726811239157d744e4254\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"Siõrškuâđam (Hidden Steps)\",\"sort_key\":\"Siõrškuâđam (Hidden Steps)\",\"short_description\":\"Laura, who grew up outside the Sámi area, walks the steps of the Sevettijärvi quadrille dance alone, as if trying to take over a language that is somehow familiar and yet foreign to her.\",\"description\":\"<p>Siõrškuâđam (Hidden Steps) is a personal story about reaching out to one's roots. Laura, who grew up outside the Sámi area, walks the steps of the Sevettijärvi quadrille dance alone, as if trying to take over a language that is somehow familiar and yet foreign to her. The steps take you to childhood memories, to a familiar path, to a familiar pine tree, to an empty Skolt farm.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1790437122863temp-1790437122757-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789691566100temp-1789691566086-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1790437122518temp-1790437122078-still.jpg\",\"trailer_url\":\"https://youtu.be/Sk7L1QCpOg0\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2025\",\"runtime\":\"13\",\"language\":\"Finnish, Skolt Sámi\",\"country\":\"Finland\",\"premiere\":\"UK\",\"instagram\":\"https://www.instagram.com/kalliokati/\",\"facebook\":\"https://www.facebook.com/katikallioArtist\",\"note\":\"Skolt Sámi\",\"subtitle_language\":\"English\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Kati Kallio, Laura Feodoroff\",\"screenwriter\":\"Kati Kallio, Laura Feodoroff\",\"producer\":\"Mete Sasioglu\",\"music\":\"Samuli Arrela, Laura Feodoroff, Aimo Aikio\",\"cast\":\"Laura Feodoroff\",\"cinematographer\":\"Arttu Peltomaa\",\"sound_design\":\"Pekka Aikio\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"62eafd839957df004bd01b7b\",\"name\":\"Short\",\"color\":\"#7fff36\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6ab7dc45292c64e36cfa2d06\",\"name\":\"Dance\",\"color\":\"#ffbc57\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"635eec67f3c9a4003067a3e2\",\"name\":\"Music Video\",\"color\":\"#fffc36\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T22:41:05.499Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-12T23:49:18.868Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true},{\"id\":\"6aa726811239157d744e4272\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"Sámi vs. Sámi\",\"sort_key\":\"Sámi vs. Sámi\",\"short_description\":\"The first documentary about a Northern Sámi vs Southern Sámi courtroom battle over land and reindeer herding in the region of Umeå.\",\"description\":\"<p>A century ago, the Norwegian and Swedish states forcibly relocated a Northern Sámi community to Tärnaby, a Southern Sámi territory — two peaceful communities, who considered themselves as one people, suddenly became embroiled in a territorial dispute.</p><p><br></p><p>Today, their descendants, Erik (Southern Sámi) and Inger Ann (Northern Sámi) face each other in court, over their rights to land, reindeer herding, and Sámi identity.</p><p><br></p><p>Sámi versus Sámi is both an intimate Sámi story, and universal drama of displacement and belonging. It speaks to Indigenous struggles everywhere, and is the director's contribution to ensuring that these stories are neither silenced nor forgotten.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789862158266temp-1789862158212-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789862306953temp-1789862306938-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789862158010temp-1789862157884-still.jpg\",\"trailer_url\":\"https://youtu.be/vmUwSah1_TA\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2026\",\"runtime\":\"77\",\"language\":\"Northern Sami, Southern Sami, Swedish\",\"country\":\"Norway, Sweden\",\"facebook\":\"https://www.facebook.com/tenthousandimages\",\"instagram\":\"https://www.instagram.com/tenthousandimages\",\"subtitle_language\":\"English\",\"note\":\"Northern Sámi, Southern Sámi\",\"premiere\":\"UK\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Ellen-Astri Lundby\",\"screenwriter\":\"Ellen-Astri Lundby\",\"producer\":\"Johanna Dorothea Raita, Mette Cheng Munthe-Kaas\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"635802d3f4bc74007700df78\",\"name\":\"Documentary\",\"color\":\"#ff8fdc\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"virtual_content\":{\"id\":\"6ab8049a96c75616628021bb\",\"type\":\"vod\",\"label\":\"sÀmi_versus_sÀmi__(eng_version).mp4\",\"status\":\"vod_transcode_failure\",\"status_description\":\"Unsupported resolution: 1920x960. <a href=\\\"https://help.eventive.org/en/articles/4028634-upload-films-on-eventive-virtual\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\">More Info</a>\",\"ev_next_encoding_id\":\"408c7091-bfaf-4834-a7e4-1ec396793cd7\",\"live_chat_visible\":true,\"live_chat_participation_enabled\":true,\"live_chat_show_viewer_count\":true,\"ams_drm_enabled\":true,\"file_size\":1991774033,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-26T17:44:58.909Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-26T17:44:58.918Z\",\"platform\":\"ev_next\",\"caption_tracks\":[]},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T22:41:05.525Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-26T18:04:37.229Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true}],\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-26T14:39:08.505Z\",\"is_virtual\":false,\"comscore_include\":true,\"geographic_restrictions\":[],\"geographic_exclusions\":[],\"vague_geographic_restrictions\":false,\"show_in_coming_soon\":false,\"allow_preorder\":false,\"aarp_member_required\":false,\"show_quantity_countdown\":false,\"virtual_balloting_enabled\":false,\"virtual_balloting_inline_during_playback\":false,\"use_default_event_bucket_preroll\":true,\"virtual_content_preroll\":[],\"virtual_content_preroll_visible\":true,\"use_default_event_bucket_postroll\":true,\"virtual_content_postroll\":[],\"virtual_content_postroll_visible\":true,\"virtual_intervals\":null,\"display_ads\":[],\"images\":{},\"ledger_tags\":[],\"rules\":[]},{\"id\":\"6ac2e7ddf511af04eef5e0a8\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"timezone\":\"Europe/London\",\"name\":\"Gods & Devils : Postindian Survivance\",\"description\":\"<p><strong style=\\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\\">Films, Talk, Poetry –&nbsp;Indigenous cinematic futurisms by Kalaallit Nunaat and Turtle Island artists.</strong></p><p><span style=\\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\\">Join us for a Saturday Shorts programme celebrating Greenlandic and Turtle Island storytellers.</span></p><p><strong style=\\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\\">In-person</strong><span style=\\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\\">: Kalaallisut artist </span><strong style=\\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\\">Dennis Inuk Aningaaq Møller </strong><span style=\\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\\">presents his Super 8 visual poetry; followed by nine Turtle Island films, including: ‘</span><em style=\\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\\">Gods &amp; Devils’</em><span style=\\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\\"> 35mm Louis Riel historical drama, </span><em style=\\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\\">‘Johnny Crow’</em><span style=\\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\\"> animated spray-painted murals, </span><em style=\\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\\">‘Lethal Ethal’</em><span style=\\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\\"> Naskapi vampirism, and Cree astronomer </span><em style=\\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\\">‘Wilfred Buck’s Star Stories’</em><span style=\\\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\\\">.</span></p>\",\"short_description\":\"\",\"venue\":{},\"is_dated\":true,\"start_time\":\"2026-11-07T13:30:00.000Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-11-07T16:30:00.000Z\",\"cutoff_event_watch_at_availability_end\":false,\"tags\":[],\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"hide_tickets_button\":false,\"require_mailing_address\":false,\"require_phone_number\":false,\"rush_line_enabled\":false,\"passholder_ticket_required\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_enabled\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_unlocked\":false,\"sales_disabled_unless_coupon\":false,\"show_custom_checkout_message\":false,\"tickets_button_label\":\"\",\"external_tickets_url\":\"https://buytickets.at/nativespiritfestival/2502706\",\"disable_pass_quick_order\":false,\"credits_disabled\":true,\"tickets_available\":true,\"unlimited\":false,\"quantity\":0,\"ticket_buckets\":[],\"films\":[{\"id\":\"6adfdc47398947eddc5d2a23\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"Visiona of Time\",\"sort_key\":\"Visiona of Time\",\"short_description\":\"Visual poetry from Kalaallit Nunaat (Greenland)\",\"description\":\"<p>An ode to less polluted days with a nostalgic longing for simpler days.</p><p>Where time is irrelevant and not caged to working hours. </p><p>A longing for days where people didn't shower themselves in perfume and kept it simple.</p><p>A longing for community in an age of isolation and a sense of belonging, </p><p>where getting help was a common sense and not something to be begged for.</p><p>A longing to protect the disappearing nature that's continually polluted.</p><p>A time where singing and practicing own traditions was normal and not seen as a crazed person.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1793056265462temp-1793056265384-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1793056429532temp-1793056429374-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1793056429189temp-1793056429041-still.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"language\":\"Kalaallisut\",\"premiere\":\"UK\",\"runtime\":\"3\",\"subtitle_language\":\"English\",\"country\":\"Kalaallit Nunaat, Greenland\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Dennis Inuk Aningaaq Møller\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"6359f247075ab6008cd35f2f\",\"name\":\"Experimental\",\"color\":\"#8d95ff\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"62eafd839957df004bd01b7b\",\"name\":\"Short\",\"color\":\"#7fff36\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-26T23:03:35.191Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-26T23:13:49.038Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true},{\"id\":\"6aa726811239157d744e4236\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"Pinngortitarlu Oqaloqatigiinneq (Dialogue With Nature)\",\"sort_key\":\"Pinngortitarlu Oqaloqatigiinneq (Dialogue With Nature)\",\"short_description\":\"Visual poetry shot on super 8, a call for action on preservation of nature.\",\"description\":\"<p>A sense of nostalgia, a taste of realness in a world of artificiality. </p><p>Sadness and longing being in between worlds, (urban and rural.) </p><p>Constant dialogue inside oneself about loss from the ancient soul, whispering in a modern world.</p><p><br></p><p>Living in this time of the world, out of touch, where slowness feels like a punishment rather than peace and attentive.</p><p><br></p><p>Dreamlike atmosphere, floaty feeling and longing in between, feeling cast away from both worlds and feeling rootless while admiring the beauty of small details.</p><p><br></p><p>A sense of euphoria and a sense of timeless peace, a connection to the ancient world. </p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789859619625temp-1789859619595-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789859690282temp-1789859690273-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789859690058temp-1789859689945-still.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2026\",\"runtime\":\"4\",\"language\":\"Kalaallisut\",\"country\":\"Greenland\",\"facebook\":\"https://www.facebook.com/dennis.k.moller/\",\"instagram\":\"https://www.instagram.com/irondennis/\",\"subtitle_language\":\"English\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Dennis Tulugaq (MÃ¸ller)\",\"screenwriter\":\"Dennis Tulugaq (MÃ¸ller)\",\"producer\":\"Dennis Tulugaq (MÃ¸ller)\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"62eafd839957df004bd01b7b\",\"name\":\"Short\",\"color\":\"#7fff36\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"62eafd6b54339000d369108b\",\"name\":\"microIndigenous\",\"color\":\"#fffc36\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T22:41:05.471Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-19T23:14:49.942Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true},{\"id\":\"6adfdeb873ea10ce6758e130\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"Elios Fovsen (Let Fovsen Live)\",\"sort_key\":\"Elios Fovsen (Let Fovsen Live)\",\"short_description\":\"Documentary segment about the protest against wind turbines at Fosen, Norway\",\"description\":\"<p>A short segment from a documentary about the demonstration in Oslo outside the Norwegian Parliament.</p><p>The protest against wind turbines at Fosen, Norway. Where the Norwegian government went above the supreme court's ruling, built the wind turbines illegally and violating human rights, including Indigenous rights, that is still ongoing.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1793057659839temp-1793057659737-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1793057415686temp-1793057415496-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1793057415299temp-1793057415084-still.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"language\":\"Kalaallisut\",\"premiere\":\"UK\",\"runtime\":\"7\",\"subtitle_language\":\"English\",\"country\":\"Norway\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Dennis Inuk Aningaaq Møller\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"635802d3f4bc74007700df78\",\"name\":\"Documentary\",\"color\":\"#ff8fdc\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"62eafd839957df004bd01b7b\",\"name\":\"Short\",\"color\":\"#7fff36\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-26T23:14:00.669Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-26T23:34:19.734Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true},{\"id\":\"6adfe3d9bdfb6926545c3f83\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"Nuna Nammineq (Land Back)\",\"sort_key\":\"Nuna Nammineq (Land Back)\",\"short_description\":\"A quiet demonstration after the orange blob started to harass us Greenlanders about a hostile takeover and casual violations.\",\"description\":\"<p>A quiet demonstration after the orange blob started to harass us Greenlanders about a hostile takeover and casual violations.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1793057785351temp-1793057785255-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1793058010953temp-1793058010780-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1793058010554temp-1793058010390-still.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"country\":\"Kalaallit Nunaat, Greenland\",\"language\":\"Kalaallisut\",\"premiere\":\"UK\",\"runtime\":\"3\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Dennis Inuk Aningaaq Møller\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"6359f247075ab6008cd35f2f\",\"name\":\"Experimental\",\"color\":\"#8d95ff\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"62eafd839957df004bd01b7b\",\"name\":\"Short\",\"color\":\"#7fff36\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-26T23:35:53.113Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-26T23:40:10.388Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true},{\"id\":\"6aa726811239157d744e4256\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"Gods & Devils\",\"sort_key\":\"Gods & Devils\",\"description\":\"<p>May 12, 1885. Batoche, Saskatchewan. Treaty 6. Canada.</p>\\n<p>With the thunder of approaching gunfire shaking the walls of the Church of Batoche, MÃ©tis legend Louis Riel delivers one last message to the men, women and children huddled inside â€” a plea for courage, a prayer for survival, and a prophecy of a future not yet written. Outside, nearly a thousand Canadian soldiers close in. Inside, Riel struggles to offer resolution and solace in the moments before the resistance, and the lives of those he swore to protect, are engulfed by violence.</p>\\n<p>This dramatic short film written and directed by Cree MÃ©tis filmmaker Jay Cardinal Villeneuve, showcases MÃ©tis and Cree actors on the screen and BIPOC talent behind the scenes, featuring stand out performances by up and coming MÃ©tis actors Cody Kearsley as Louis Riel, Shane Leydon as Gabriel Dumont and Jillian Dion (from Killers of the Flower Moon) as Marguerite Riel Monet performing in Michif, as well as Production Design by MÃ©tis artist Cheryl Marion, a haunting original score by the NDN Cowboy himself Wayne Lavallee whom you'd know from Bones of Crows, and 35mm cinematography by MÃ©tis/Japanese DP Kaayla Whachell. It was also produced by MÃ©tis producer Greg Coyes and Haudenosaunee producer/filmmaker Jessie Anthony.</p>\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789689938011temp-1789689937998-poster.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2025\",\"runtime\":\"12\",\"language\":\"Cree, French\",\"country\":\"Canada\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Jay Cardinal Villeneuve\",\"screenwriter\":\"Jay Cardinal Villeneuve\",\"producer\":\"Greg Coyes, Jessie Anthony\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T22:41:05.500Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-18T00:05:37.996Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true},{\"id\":\"6aa726811239157d744e425e\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"MONSTR\",\"sort_key\":\"MONSTR\",\"description\":\"<p>How do you go on living when everything is taken from you in the blink of an eye? </p><p><br></p><p>A young artist confronts his inner demons while apprenticing with a northwest totem carver after the death of his beloved.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789863498816temp-1789863498760-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789863504646temp-1789863504637-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789863504422temp-1789863504296-still.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2023\",\"runtime\":\"6\",\"language\":\"English\",\"country\":\"Canada\",\"instagram\":\"https://www.instagram.com/puppet_flogger/\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Tank Standing Buffalo\",\"screenwriter\":\"Tank Standing Buffalo, Xstine Cook\",\"producer\":\"Xstine Cook, Amanda Miller\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"62eafd839957df004bd01b7b\",\"name\":\"Short\",\"color\":\"#7fff36\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"62eafd6b54339000d369108b\",\"name\":\"microIndigenous\",\"color\":\"#fffc36\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T22:41:05.508Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-20T00:18:24.293Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true},{\"id\":\"6aa726811239157d744e4296\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"Lethal Ethel\",\"sort_key\":\"Lethal Ethel\",\"description\":\"<p>Blending horror and humour, Lethal Ethel is a mockumentary that follows the story of a Naskapi vampire who goes to murderous lengths to protect her land and culture.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789852177993temp-1789852177971-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789852149779temp-1789852149768-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789852149522temp-1789852149484-still.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2025\",\"runtime\":\"8\",\"country\":\"Canada\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Elayna Einish\",\"screenwriter\":\"Elayna Einish, Dan Boos, Rui Silveira\",\"producer\":\"Wapikoni mobile\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"62eafd839957df004bd01b7b\",\"name\":\"Short\",\"color\":\"#7fff36\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T22:41:05.558Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-19T21:09:37.969Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true},{\"id\":\"6aa726811239157d744e4260\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"Johnny Crow\",\"sort_key\":\"Johnny Crow\",\"description\":\"<p>A poetic and transformative journey of a young man’s physical, mental, and spiritual struggle to return to his son through the criminal justice system and the layers of colonization it represents. </p><p><br></p><p>Created by animating spray-painted murals frame-by-frame, Cree artist Jesse Gouchey painted each frame on large outdoor surfaces over a period of seven years in numerous locations across Alberta and BC. </p><p><br></p><p>Johnny Crow's struggle speaks to the resilience of modern day warriors surviving and resisting bureaucratic battles of written laws vs oral traditions, and is contrasted by a haunting poem written and performed by spoken word artist Mitcholos Touchie. </p><p><br></p><p>Turtle Island agreements were to share, and nobody was conquered. Today's resistance seeks to expose and correct treaty trickery, the dishonourable paper wars that are won and lost with the flick of a stock market digit.</p><p><br></p><p>Spoken word: Mitcholos Touchie (Hitacu, Yuułuʔiłʔatḥ x Nuučaan̓uɫ)</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789852007961temp-1789852007937-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789852008159temp-1789852008143-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789852007708temp-1789852007590-still.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2021\",\"runtime\":\"7\",\"language\":\"English\",\"country\":\"Canada\",\"facebook\":\"https://www.facebook.com/Johnny-Crow-109649412493125\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Xstine Cook, Jesse Gouchey\",\"screenwriter\":\"Xstine Cook, Jesse Gouchey, Mitcholos Touchie\",\"producer\":\"Xstine Cook\",\"music\":\"Bullhorn Singers (Kainai), Billy Wadsworth (Kainai), Celina Kalluk (Inuit-Canadian), Daniel Neary, Pura Fé (Tuscarora), Cary L. Morin, Antonia Crescioni\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T22:41:05.509Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-19T21:06:47.588Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true},{\"id\":\"6aa726811239157d744e4298\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"Call me Crazy One More Time\",\"sort_key\":\"Call me Crazy One More Time\",\"description\":\"<p>A performance poem by Danielle Vandale, a MÃ©tis artist from Saskatchewan, Call Me Crazy One More Time sheds light on the devastating effects of prescription psychiatric drugs: the inability to feel emotions of motherhood and of tragically losing her daughter. Calling out the medical and social services system that Indigenous mothers must navigate all too often without support, understanding or hope, the director calls for a change in the way Indigenous women are treated.</p>\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789689246534temp-1789689246520-poster.jpg\",\"trailer_url\":\"https://youtu.be/4yyH7TgjFFA\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2025\",\"runtime\":\"5\",\"country\":\"Canada\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Danielle Vandale\",\"producer\":\"Wapikoni mobile\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T22:41:05.560Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T23:54:42.658Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true},{\"id\":\"6aa726811239157d744e429c\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"On Postindian Survivance\",\"sort_key\":\"On Postindian Survivance\",\"short_description\":\"A work of art refusing settler colonial representation politics yet espousing relationality as its core tenet, built upon the work of emerging artist and sonic warrior Emcee Sioui. .\",\"description\":\"<p>On Postindian Survivance is an experimental clip/short film built upon the work of emerging artist and sonic warrior Emcee Sioui. It is but a work of art refusing settler colonial representation politics yet espousing relationality as its core tenet.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789682780780temp-1789682780756-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789682780979temp-1789682780964-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789682780542temp-1789682780441-still.jpg\",\"trailer_url\":\"https://youtu.be/xj-HhEIHfas\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2026\",\"runtime\":\"5\",\"language\":\"English\",\"country\":\"Canada\",\"note\":\"Wendat, Wendake\",\"premiere\":\"World\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Sioui One\",\"screenwriter\":\"Sioui One\",\"producer\":\"Wapikoni Mobile\",\"cast\":\"Sioui One\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"62eafd839957df004bd01b7b\",\"name\":\"Short\",\"color\":\"#7fff36\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"62eafd6b54339000d369108b\",\"name\":\"microIndigenous\",\"color\":\"#fffc36\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6359f247075ab6008cd35f2f\",\"name\":\"Experimental\",\"color\":\"#8d95ff\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"virtual_content\":{\"id\":\"6aac5c849bb2369fc4da032e\",\"type\":\"vod\",\"label\":\"STA - On Postindian Survivance.mp4\",\"status\":\"ready\",\"status_percent\":100,\"ev_next_encoding_id\":\"6a199863-20fb-4218-be06-195705d05c69\",\"live_chat_visible\":true,\"live_chat_participation_enabled\":true,\"live_chat_show_viewer_count\":true,\"ams_drm_enabled\":true,\"duration\":302165.333,\"file_size\":829657771,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-17T21:32:52.221Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T21:32:52.234Z\",\"platform\":\"ev_next\",\"caption_tracks\":[]},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T22:41:05.563Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T22:06:20.440Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true},{\"id\":\"6aa726811239157d744e4242\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"TOTEM\",\"sort_key\":\"TOTEM\",\"description\":\"<p>Ashley Harrah is a \\\"pretendian\\\" falsely claiming Native American heritage to boost her popularity as an online influencer. Her latest video takes her on a vision quest for a sacred totem pole she discovers is cursed, not sacred.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789692657613temp-1789692657545-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789692611980temp-1789692611969-poster.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2025\",\"runtime\":\"21\",\"language\":\"English\",\"country\":\"United States\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"That Native Thomas\",\"screenwriter\":\"That Native Thomas\",\"producer\":\"Mandy Yeahpau\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"62eafd839957df004bd01b7b\",\"name\":\"Short\",\"color\":\"#7fff36\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6359f247075ab6008cd35f2f\",\"name\":\"Experimental\",\"color\":\"#8d95ff\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T22:41:05.482Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-18T00:51:19.614Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true},{\"id\":\"6aa726811239157d744e4220\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"Ñuuyii (Earth)\",\"sort_key\":\"Ñuuyii (Earth)\",\"description\":\"<p>A young man, born and raised in the vastness of the galaxy, lands on an unknown planet. As he surveys the landscape, he encounters an abandoned city, an overgrown cemetery, and lush vegetation.  Driven by a quiet urgency, he contacts his shipâ€™s command to retrieve archival recordings of the last humans to abandon earth. Slowly, it dawns on him there is something familiar about the place. </p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789687162550temp-1789687162507-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789687162764temp-1789687162753-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789687047731temp-1789687047610-still.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2025\",\"runtime\":\"11\",\"language\":\"English\",\"country\":\"Mexico, United Kingdom\",\"twitter\":\"https://www.twitter.com/calistafilms\",\"instagram\":\"https://www.instagram.com/armando_listacalistafilms\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Itandehui Jansen\",\"screenwriter\":\"Itandehui Jansen, Armando Bautista Garcia\",\"producer\":\"Armando Bautista GarcÃ­a\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"62eafd839957df004bd01b7b\",\"name\":\"Short\",\"color\":\"#7fff36\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6535f06ea45954004707d11c\",\"name\":\"Sci-Fi\",\"color\":\"#ffbc57\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T22:41:05.446Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T23:19:22.505Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true},{\"id\":\"6aa726811239157d744e422a\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"Wilfred Buck's Star Stories\",\"sort_key\":\"Wilfred Buck's Star Stories\",\"description\":\"<p>Designed for presentation in domes and planetariums, this 21-minute XR work brings to life four star stories, gathered and told by renowned Ininew (Cree) astronomer/star knowledge expert and author Wilfred Buck. From the practical to the poetic, these \\\"tellings\\\" of the Northern night sky provide guidance on navigation, the earth’s cycles, and how to live a good life with future generations in mind. WILFRED BUCK'S STAR STORIES offers a rarely heard perspective on astronomy and cosmology in an immersive and intimate environment for participants.</p><p><br></p><p>Marvel at immersive night sky cinematography, cosmos CGI, and beautiful macro cinematography of meteorites set to a transporting soundtrack in this expansive yet intimate experience that combines the wonder of the universe with the warmth of listening to a wise Elder whose teachings can help us understand that the stars are in fact our oldest relatives.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789864547806temp-1789864547775-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789864548045temp-1789864548028-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789864525824temp-1789864525717-still.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2025\",\"runtime\":\"20\",\"language\":\"Cree, English, French\",\"country\":\"Canada\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Lisa Jackson\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T22:41:05.459Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-20T00:35:47.773Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true}],\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-30T19:43:57.522Z\",\"is_virtual\":false,\"comscore_include\":true,\"geographic_restrictions\":[],\"geographic_exclusions\":[],\"vague_geographic_restrictions\":false,\"show_in_coming_soon\":false,\"allow_preorder\":false,\"aarp_member_required\":false,\"show_quantity_countdown\":false,\"virtual_balloting_enabled\":false,\"virtual_balloting_inline_during_playback\":false,\"use_default_event_bucket_preroll\":true,\"virtual_content_preroll\":[],\"virtual_content_preroll_visible\":true,\"use_default_event_bucket_postroll\":true,\"virtual_content_postroll\":[],\"virtual_content_postroll_visible\":true,\"virtual_intervals\":null,\"display_ads\":[],\"images\":{},\"ledger_tags\":[],\"rules\":[]},{\"id\":\"6ab9623fc412a084ccbfbba5\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"timezone\":\"Europe/London\",\"name\":\"Uma Memória Emplumada, A Feathered Memory & Forgotten Founder: The Untold Story of Samson Occom and Dartmouth\",\"description\":\"\",\"short_description\":\"\",\"location\":\"IALS Council Chamber Theatre\",\"venue\":{\"id\":\"6ab9626b0628e5a5a8ce84d3\",\"name\":\"IALS Council Chamber Theatre\",\"short_name\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"address\":\"Institute of Advanced Legal Studies, Charles Clore House, 17 Russell Sq, London WC1B 5DR\",\"default_capacity\":100,\"color\":\"#ff8fdc\",\"use_reserved_seating\":false,\"comscore_include\":false},\"is_dated\":true,\"start_time\":\"2026-11-11T18:00:00.000Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-11-11T21:00:00.000Z\",\"cutoff_event_watch_at_availability_end\":false,\"tags\":[],\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"hide_tickets_button\":false,\"require_mailing_address\":false,\"require_phone_number\":false,\"rush_line_enabled\":false,\"passholder_ticket_required\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_enabled\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_unlocked\":false,\"sales_disabled_unless_coupon\":false,\"show_custom_checkout_message\":false,\"tickets_button_label\":\"\",\"external_tickets_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/native-spirit-festival-20th-edition-world-indigenous-led-cinema-tickets-2001782208472\",\"disable_pass_quick_order\":false,\"credits_disabled\":true,\"tickets_available\":true,\"unlimited\":false,\"quantity\":0,\"ticket_buckets\":[],\"films\":[{\"id\":\"6aa726811239157d744e425a\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"Uma Memória Emplumada, A Feathered Memory\",\"sort_key\":\"Uma Memória Emplumada, A Feathered Memory\",\"description\":\"<p>A Feathered Memory (Uma Memória Emplumada) is a poetic documentary directed and produced by Ida Does. The film follows Brazilian Indigenous artist and human rights activist Daiara Tukano, a member of the Tukano people of the Amazon, as she creates a monumental mural at the Mauritshuis in The Hague.</p><p><br></p><p>As the mural slowly emerges on the museum walls, a deeper story unfolds — one that connects the colonial history of the Netherlands with the living knowledge, spirituality, and resistance of the Indigenous peoples of the Amazon. Through intimate encounters, reflections, and fragments of Tukano’s poem To Be Forest, the film explores the role of art as a bridge between cultures and as a tool for healing historical wounds.</p><p><br></p><p>The narrative moves between The Hague and Brazil, where Tukano reflects on the relationship between art, memory, and the defense of Indigenous territories. A powerful thread in the film is the story of the sacred Tupinambá feather mantle, a ceremonial object made of thousands of red ibis feathers that was taken to Europe during the colonial period and recently returned to Brazil. The mantle becomes a symbol of restitution, ancestral memory, and cultural survival.</p><p><br></p><p>Combining lyrical cinematography, archival echoes, and Tukano’s voice, A Feathered Memory invites viewers to reconsider how museums, colonial histories, and Indigenous perspectives intersect today. The film is both a reflection on the power of art and a tribute to the resilience of Indigenous cultures.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789858918054temp-1789858918005-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789858918299temp-1789858918284-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789858856764temp-1789858856718-still.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2025\",\"runtime\":\"56\",\"language\":\"Dutch, English, Portuguese\",\"country\":\"Netherlands\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"ida does, milton kam, emile vd griendt, bernardo bravo, jeroen nadorp\",\"screenwriter\":\"ida does\",\"producer\":\"ida does\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"635802d3f4bc74007700df78\",\"name\":\"Documentary\",\"color\":\"#ff8fdc\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T22:41:05.504Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-19T23:01:58.002Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true},{\"id\":\"6aa726811239157d744e425c\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"Forgotten Founder: The Untold Story of Samson Occom and Dartmouth\",\"sort_key\":\"Forgotten Founder: The Untold Story of Samson Occom and Dartmouth\",\"description\":\"<p>Co-directed by Melissa Tantaquidgeon Zobel, a descendant of Occom, and filmmaker Signe Taylor, this new documentary uncovers the largely erased history of Samson Occom, a Mohegan minister, educator and Indigenous intellectual whose fundraising efforts were instrumental in the founding of Dartmouth College. Despite his central role, Occom's contributions—and the promises made to Native communities—were erased from the historical record.</p><p><br></p><p>The film features three of Occom's descendants—Sarah Harris, Vice Chair of the Mohegan Tribal Council and the first Mohegan woman to graduate from Dartmouth; Beth Regan, Native Studies educator and Chair of Mohegan's Council of Elders; and Bruce Bozsum, a well-regarded actor playing Occom's spirit and a member of the Council of Elders—creating a powerful dialogue between history, memory, and lived experience. Bringing together leading scholars—including Dartmouth Professor Bruce Duthu and Indigenous Scholar Anthony Trujillo—archival materials, and community voices, the film explores questions of legacy, accountability, and survival.</p><p><br></p><p>As the United States approaches its 250th anniversary, the film arrives at a critical moment. In an era when history itself is fiercely contested, Forgotten Founder calls for a fuller, more honest reckoning with America's origins—one that acknowledges Indigenous presence, contribution and resilience, and insists that these stories be restored to the center of our national memory.</p>\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789690045392temp-1789690045382-poster.jpg\",\"trailer_url\":\"https://youtu.be/bK3ahUVPqGk\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2026\",\"runtime\":\"29\",\"language\":\"English\",\"country\":\"United States\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Signe Margueritte Taylor, Melissa Tantaquidgeon Zobel\",\"screenwriter\":\"Melissa Tantaquidgeon Zobel\",\"producer\":\"R. Michael Murray, Sarah Harris, Beth Regan, Justin Anderson, Susanne Mehrer, Kathryn Kennedy\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T22:41:05.506Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-18T00:08:36.906Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true},{\"id\":\"6aa726811239157d744e4266\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"Bringing His Spirit Home\",\"sort_key\":\"Bringing His Spirit Home\",\"description\":\"<p>Peter’s great-uncle, an Aboriginal WWI soldier, is buried far away from his family and traditional lands. With a cultural belief that his ancestor’s spirit won’t be at rest until he returns home, Peter travels to France to visit his grave, performing a traditional ceremony to bring his spirit home.</p>\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789689046234temp-1789689046223-poster.jpg\",\"trailer_url\":\"https://youtu.be/NdV5pWAXWtw\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2025\",\"runtime\":\"13\",\"language\":\"English, French\",\"country\":\"Australia\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Dylan Nicholls\",\"producer\":\"Sophia Carolyn Wallace, Dylan Nicholls\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T22:41:05.515Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T23:51:49.751Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true}],\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-27T19:24:16.692Z\",\"is_virtual\":false,\"comscore_include\":true,\"geographic_restrictions\":[],\"geographic_exclusions\":[],\"vague_geographic_restrictions\":false,\"show_in_coming_soon\":false,\"allow_preorder\":false,\"aarp_member_required\":false,\"show_quantity_countdown\":false,\"virtual_balloting_enabled\":false,\"virtual_balloting_inline_during_playback\":false,\"use_default_event_bucket_preroll\":true,\"virtual_content_preroll\":[],\"virtual_content_preroll_visible\":true,\"use_default_event_bucket_postroll\":true,\"virtual_content_postroll\":[],\"virtual_content_postroll_visible\":true,\"virtual_intervals\":null,\"display_ads\":[],\"images\":{},\"ledger_tags\":[],\"rules\":[]},{\"id\":\"6ac2e6efa708fca891c6ba80\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"timezone\":\"Europe/London\",\"name\":\"Illustrated Legacies: Graveyard of the Pacific\",\"description\":\"\",\"short_description\":\"\",\"location\":\"IALS Council Chamber Theatre\",\"venue\":{\"id\":\"6ab9626b0628e5a5a8ce84d3\",\"name\":\"IALS Council Chamber Theatre\",\"short_name\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"address\":\"Institute of Advanced Legal Studies, Charles Clore House, 17 Russell Sq, London WC1B 5DR\",\"default_capacity\":100,\"color\":\"#ff8fdc\",\"use_reserved_seating\":false,\"comscore_include\":false},\"is_dated\":true,\"start_time\":\"2026-11-14T12:00:00.000Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-11-14T21:00:00.000Z\",\"cutoff_event_watch_at_availability_end\":false,\"tags\":[],\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"hide_tickets_button\":false,\"require_mailing_address\":false,\"require_phone_number\":false,\"rush_line_enabled\":false,\"passholder_ticket_required\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_enabled\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_unlocked\":false,\"sales_disabled_unless_coupon\":false,\"show_custom_checkout_message\":false,\"external_tickets_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/native-spirit-festival-20th-edition-world-indigenous-led-cinema-ii-tickets-2001782570555\",\"disable_pass_quick_order\":false,\"credits_disabled\":true,\"tickets_available\":true,\"unlimited\":false,\"quantity\":0,\"ticket_buckets\":[],\"films\":[{\"id\":\"6aa726811239157d744e4244\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"Illustrated Legacies: Graveyard of the Pacific\",\"sort_key\":\"Illustrated Legacies: Graveyard of the Pacific\",\"description\":\"<p>Illustrated Legacies: Graveyard of the Pacific reclaims coastal Indigenous history, tracing a continuum from ancient whaling practices to the upheaval of colonial conflict. Relying on oral traditions, and combining documentary form with animation, the film challenges mainstream eurocentric narratives centering instead the vibrant lives and cultures of the original stewards of the lands and ocean. Through this lens a complicated history is reframed by the voices of the Indigenous Peoples of Canada’s west coast.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789851694733temp-1789851694710-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789851747855temp-1789851747845-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789851747607temp-1789851747510-still.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2026\",\"runtime\":\"10\",\"language\":\"English\",\"country\":\"Canada\",\"instagram\":\"https://www.instagram.com/twohoundsmedia/?hl=en\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Tanner Zurkoski\",\"screenwriter\":\"Tanner Zurkoski\",\"producer\":\"Tanner Zurkoski\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T22:41:05.484Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-19T21:02:27.508Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true},{\"id\":\"6aa726811239157d744e426c\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"Namesake təm kʷaθ nan\",\"sort_key\":\"Namesake təm kʷaθ nan\",\"description\":\"<p>təm kʷaθ nan Namesake documents an ongoing conversation between the Tla’amin Nation and the city commonly known as Powell River.</p><p><br></p><p>The city’s name honours Israel Wood Powell, a government official whose policies helped establish residential schools, criminalize cultural practices, and remove Tla’amin from its home at tiskʷət. The Tla’amin Nation asks the city to consider changing its name, not to erase history but to build a new future together.</p><p><br></p><p>This request sparks public meetings, emotional testimony, resistance and outrage, allyship, and reflection across the region. Elders share naming traditions that connect people with history, land and responsibility. Archaeological evidence reveals over 12,000 years of continuous Tla’amin presence. Current residents grapple with family history, belonging, and fears of losing identity. </p><p><br></p><p>The outcome remains uncertain. The conversation itself becomes the story.</p><p>Following the Tla’amin seasonal cycle, the film observes how communities change slowly through listening, disagreement, repair, and time.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789864358194temp-1789864358140-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789864233475temp-1789864233462-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789864357924temp-1789864357792-still.jpg\",\"trailer_url\":\"https://youtu.be/SkNHNO9KX8Q\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2026\",\"runtime\":\"76\",\"language\":\"English\",\"country\":\"Canada\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Evan ƛɛsla Adams, Eileen t̓agəm Francis\",\"screenwriter\":\"Peg Campbell, Angela Kendall\",\"producer\":\"Peg Campbell\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"62eafd839957df004bd01b7b\",\"name\":\"Short\",\"color\":\"#7fff36\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"635802d3f4bc74007700df78\",\"name\":\"Documentary\",\"color\":\"#ff8fdc\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T22:41:05.520Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-26T22:47:32.631Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true},{\"id\":\"6aa726811239157d744e423e\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"She Cried That Day\",\"sort_key\":\"She Cried That Day\",\"short_description\":\"SHE CRIED THAT DAY is a story of love, spirit and the unwavering power of Indigenous Women who refuse to let their loved ones remain invisible in the eyes of the justice system.\",\"description\":\"<p>SHE CRIED THAT DAY exposes a crisis hiding in plain sight through the eyes of those on the frontlines. Christine Means and her family have spent years questioning the circumstances surrounding her sister's death. In 2019, a renewed sense of hope for justice places Christine at the center of the Missing and Murdered Indigenous Women and Relatives movement in New Mexico. As she becomes a voice for her sister, we get an inside look into how this deadly crisis takes a toll on a family, a community and a state.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789859199077temp-1789859199034-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789859059175temp-1789859059163-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789859198810temp-1789859198681-still.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2025\",\"runtime\":\"31\",\"language\":\"English\",\"country\":\"United States\",\"facebook\":\"https://facebook.com/seesclearlyproductions\",\"instagram\":\"https://instagram.com/seesclearlyproductions\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Amanda Erickson\",\"producer\":\"Tracy Rector, Stina Thomas Hamlin\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"635802d3f4bc74007700df78\",\"name\":\"Documentary\",\"color\":\"#ff8fdc\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T22:41:05.479Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-19T23:06:38.678Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true},{\"id\":\"6aa726811239157d744e4222\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"KIN - Dudi & Jojo\",\"sort_key\":\"KIN - Dudi & Jojo\",\"short_description\":\"KIN is a collection of poetic documentaries produced by Outer Urban Projects that reveal the profound musical families and subcultures within Naarm/Melbourne's outer northern diasporic communities.\",\"description\":\"<p>Produced by Outer Urban Projects, directed and animated by Tumeli Tuqota, KIN - Dudi &amp; Jojo is the first in the KIN film series.</p><p><br></p><p>This film sees iTaukei Fijian-Australian vocalists and twin sisters Ruci (Dudi) Kaisila and Joanne (Jojo) Kaisila debut as writers and filmmakers, exploring their deeply personal insights into Fiji, its culture, the diaspora and their lives as burgeoning cultural custodians and singers in a Gospel family.</p><p><br></p><p>A story of ancestral consciousness told in animation and live action.</p><p><br></p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789686290807temp-1789686290759-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789686148002temp-1789686147988-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789686147757temp-1789686147616-still.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2025\",\"runtime\":\"25\",\"language\":\"English, Fijian\",\"country\":\"Australia\",\"facebook\":\"https://www.facebook.com/outerurbanprojects\",\"instagram\":\"https://www.instagram.com/outerurban/\",\"note\":\"iTaukei Fijian-Australian.Joseph Baro-Kaurasi - Masi Pattern Artist, Taleivini Kaimacuata Illustrator \",\"premiere\":\"Europe\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Tumeli Tuqota\",\"screenwriter\":\"Ruci Kaisila, Joanne Kaisila, Tumeli Tuqota\",\"producer\":\"Kate Gillick, Irine Vela\",\"animator\":\"Tumeli Tuqota\",\"cinematographer\":\"Miguel Rios, Meredith O'Shea\",\"composer\":\"Ruci Kaisila, Joanne Kaisila\",\"editor\":\"Dave Lavaki Laisiasa\",\"music\":\"Ruci Kaisila\",\"production_design\":\"Calysta Morgan, Dani Niuatau\",\"sound_design\":\"Irine Vela\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"62eafd839957df004bd01b7b\",\"name\":\"Short\",\"color\":\"#7fff36\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"635825d51e5f71006a124690\",\"name\":\"Animation\",\"color\":\"#8dffe7\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6359f247075ab6008cd35f2f\",\"name\":\"Experimental\",\"color\":\"#8d95ff\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T22:41:05.449Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T23:04:50.757Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true}],\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-28T22:37:30.484Z\",\"is_virtual\":false,\"comscore_include\":true,\"geographic_restrictions\":[],\"geographic_exclusions\":[],\"vague_geographic_restrictions\":false,\"show_in_coming_soon\":false,\"allow_preorder\":false,\"aarp_member_required\":false,\"show_quantity_countdown\":false,\"virtual_balloting_enabled\":false,\"virtual_balloting_inline_during_playback\":false,\"use_default_event_bucket_preroll\":true,\"virtual_content_preroll\":[],\"virtual_content_preroll_visible\":true,\"use_default_event_bucket_postroll\":true,\"virtual_content_postroll\":[],\"virtual_content_postroll_visible\":true,\"virtual_intervals\":null,\"display_ads\":[],\"images\":{},\"ledger_tags\":[],\"rules\":[]},{\"id\":\"6ab816f5d49d67faa66d9143\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"timezone\":\"Europe/London\",\"name\":\"Mundurukü – The Forest of The Fish Women\",\"description\":\"<p>Screening of five short experimental films&nbsp;with introduction&nbsp;+ writing responses activation, followed by feature <strong>Mundurukü – The Forest of The Fish Women</strong>.&nbsp;The event will be contributing&nbsp;programming of 40 minutes of experimental short films by Indigenous filmmakers whose work explores themes of ancestry and identity, while looking at how these filmmakers address&nbsp;maintaining traditions, practices and belief systems in the future.&nbsp;Alongside the screening of these shorts will be an introduction (possible video introduction), writing activation in response to the short films.</p><p><em style=\\\"background-color: transparent;\\\">Writing activation and Short films programmed by Zain Gibson </em></p>\",\"short_description\":\"\",\"location\":\"The Horse Hospital\",\"venue\":{\"id\":\"6ab8187c90b146db219585f4\",\"name\":\"The Horse Hospital\",\"short_name\":\"HH\",\"description\":\"Central London arts venue celebrating the work of underground and avant-garde artists through exhibitions, events, talks, film and music and performance.\",\"address\":\"Colonnade, London WC1N 1JD\",\"default_capacity\":null,\"color\":\"#cef2ec\",\"use_reserved_seating\":false,\"comscore_include\":false},\"is_dated\":true,\"start_time\":\"2026-11-15T13:30:00.000Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-11-15T16:30:00.000Z\",\"cutoff_event_watch_at_availability_end\":false,\"tags\":[],\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"hide_tickets_button\":false,\"require_mailing_address\":false,\"require_phone_number\":false,\"rush_line_enabled\":false,\"passholder_ticket_required\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_enabled\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_unlocked\":false,\"sales_disabled_unless_coupon\":false,\"show_custom_checkout_message\":false,\"tickets_button_label\":\"\",\"external_tickets_url\":\"https://buytickets.at/nativespiritfestival/2502815\",\"disable_pass_quick_order\":false,\"credits_disabled\":true,\"tickets_available\":true,\"unlimited\":false,\"quantity\":0,\"ticket_buckets\":[],\"films\":[{\"id\":\"6aa726811239157d744e4250\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"MUNDURUKUYÜ – THE FOREST OF THE FISH WOMEN\",\"sort_key\":\"MUNDURUKUYÜ – THE FOREST OF THE FISH WOMEN\",\"description\":\"<p>On the banks of the Tapajós River, in the Amazon, the forest of fish women reflects Mundurukü mythology, where humans, at the origin of the world, transformed into forest, plants and animals. In the daily life of the Sawre Muybu village, the spirits of the forest are not only ancestral spiritual forces, but part of the family.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789863986514temp-1789863986467-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789863986724temp-1789863986713-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789863930635temp-1789863930596-still.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2025\",\"runtime\":\"72\",\"language\":\"Portuguese\",\"country\":\"Brazil\",\"subtitle_language\":\"Mundurukü, Portuguese\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Aldira Akay, Beka Munduruku, RilcÃ©lia Akay\",\"screenwriter\":\"Aldira Akay, Beka Munduruku, EstÃªvÃ£o Ciavatta, RilcÃ©lia Akay\",\"producer\":\"Estêvão Ciavatta, Renata Carpenter, Carolina Ribas\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"635afe1ef81fd8006201a191\",\"name\":\"Feature\",\"color\":\"#608ea4\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"635825d51e5f71006a124690\",\"name\":\"Animation\",\"color\":\"#8dffe7\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T22:41:05.495Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-26T22:15:50.418Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true},{\"id\":\"6aa726811239157d744e422e\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"The Song of the Moon: A Tupinambá Story\",\"sort_key\":\"Song of the Moon: A Tupinambá Story, The\",\"short_description\":\"In the depths of a moonless night, a Tupinambá village lies dormant under an unsettling silence. When a curious young girl approaches the elders gathered around the dying embers, the village shaman breaks the void by shaking his sacred maracá.\",\"description\":\"<p>In the depths of a moonless night, a Tupinambá village lies dormant under an unsettling silence. Time seems suspended between dense shadows and the artificial glow of screens that hypnotize the younger generation. Children sleep cradled by cell phones while the ancestral fire at the communal hearth barely flickers.</p><p><br></p><p>When a curious young girl approaches the elders gathered around the dying embers, the village shaman breaks the void by shaking his sacred maracá. His rhythmic beat resonates like the earth's heartbeat, awakening forgotten memories as he chants to JACY (the Moon) and TUPÃ (God), calling not only the people but also the moon and nature itself to celebrate life.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1790608499027temp-1790608498984-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789861939724temp-1789861939711-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1790608519812temp-1790608519695-still.jpg\",\"trailer_url\":\"https://youtu.be/3cgJ-wvaTO0\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2025\",\"runtime\":\"4\",\"language\":\"Portuguese\",\"country\":\"Brazil\",\"premiere\":\"UK\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Sebastian Gerlic\",\"screenwriter\":\"Atã Xohã Tupinambá, Mbo’essara Tupinambá, Potyra Tê Tupinambá, Nynhã Gwarini Tupinambá, Kamaywha Tupinambá \",\"producer\":\"Kamaywha Tupinambá\",\"cast\":\"Chapéu Tupinambá, Laly Tupinambá, Kamaywha Tupinambá\",\"executive_producer\":\"Atã Xohã Tupinambá, Kamaywha Tupinambá\",\"production_design\":\"André Da Costa (AI Stylization)\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"62eafd839957df004bd01b7b\",\"name\":\"Short\",\"color\":\"#7fff36\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"62eafd6b54339000d369108b\",\"name\":\"microIndigenous\",\"color\":\"#fffc36\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T22:41:05.463Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-28T15:15:19.693Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true},{\"id\":\"6aa726811239157d744e428a\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"Akababuru: Expression of astonishment\",\"sort_key\":\"Akababuru: Expression of astonishment\",\"description\":\"<p>Kari, an indigenous girl who is afraid to laugh, meets Kera, who shares with her the myth of Kiraparamia, a woman punished by the gods for laughing at her husband. Kera reinterprets this and tells her that laughing set her free. Inspired, Kari uses laughter to confront those who bother her. </p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789687409524temp-1789687409487-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789687373119temp-1789687373103-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789687372864temp-1789687372746-still.jpg\",\"trailer_url\":\"https://youtu.be/pbmKreODW-M\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2025\",\"runtime\":\"13\",\"language\":\"Other\",\"country\":\"Colombia\",\"instagram\":\"https://www.instagram.com/luminti_colectivo/\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Irati Dojura Landa YagarÃ­\",\"screenwriter\":\"Irati Dojura Landa YagarÃ­\",\"producer\":\"Laura Giraldo Mira\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"62eafd839957df004bd01b7b\",\"name\":\"Short\",\"color\":\"#7fff36\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"6359f247075ab6008cd35f2f\",\"name\":\"Experimental\",\"color\":\"#8d95ff\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T22:41:05.548Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-17T23:23:29.484Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true},{\"id\":\"6aa726811239157d744e429a\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"Nimik\",\"sort_key\":\"Nimik\",\"description\":\"<p>Laurence, an artist-poet, tackles the theme of identity in this video-poem. Nimiku is a pictorial setting of three texts from her collection of the same name.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789863331091temp-1789863331032-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789863229397temp-1789863229384-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789863330827temp-1789863330784-still.jpg\",\"trailer_url\":\"https://youtu.be/DZjoEI6m3dA\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2026\",\"runtime\":\"3\",\"language\":\"French\",\"country\":\"Canada\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Laurence Vollant-Vachon\",\"screenwriter\":\"Laurence Vollant-Vachon\",\"producer\":\"Wapikoni Mobile\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"62eafd839957df004bd01b7b\",\"name\":\"Short\",\"color\":\"#7fff36\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"62eafd6b54339000d369108b\",\"name\":\"microIndigenous\",\"color\":\"#fffc36\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"virtual_content\":{\"id\":\"6ab81b41cdf2a2faa639c0b7\",\"type\":\"vod\",\"label\":\"STA - NIMIK.mp4\",\"status\":\"ready\",\"status_percent\":100,\"ev_next_encoding_id\":\"5eb313f5-c9eb-4e0b-8a5b-0091476a2a1f\",\"live_chat_visible\":true,\"live_chat_participation_enabled\":true,\"live_chat_show_viewer_count\":true,\"ams_drm_enabled\":true,\"duration\":210453.33299999998,\"file_size\":479500388,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-26T19:21:37.113Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-26T19:21:37.123Z\",\"platform\":\"ev_next\",\"caption_tracks\":[]},\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T22:41:05.561Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-26T19:03:09.812Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true},{\"id\":\"6aa726811239157d744e4276\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"Corn Husk Doll\",\"sort_key\":\"Corn Husk Doll\",\"short_description\":\"A traditional Hodinöhsö:ni' (Iroquois) legend in the Gayogohó꞉nǫʼ (Cayuga) language.\",\"description\":\"<p>Corn Husk Doll tells the story of a young, beautiful girl who neglects her community responsibilities. Despite warnings from the animals, she becomes distracted by her own reflection and slowly begins to turn into a corn husk doll with no face. This story reminds us to be humble, and to fulfill our responsibilities to our families, clan, and community.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1790457936283temp-1790457936253-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789689438390temp-1789689438367-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789689438152temp-1789689438037-still.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2025\",\"runtime\":\"14\",\"language\":\"Gayogohó꞉nǫʼ, Cayuga\",\"country\":\"Canada\",\"facebook\":\"https://www.facebook.com/BawaadanCollective/\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Yuma Dean Hester (Anishinaabe/Cree)\",\"screenwriter\":\"Kaniehtenhawi Deer Kaniehtenhawi Deer (Mohawk of Six Nations), Ben Hill, Jessica Martin, Tracy Deer\",\"producer\":\"Yuma Dean Hester, Ashley Maracle Ashley Maracle (Mohawk of Tyendinaga)\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"62eafd839957df004bd01b7b\",\"name\":\"Short\",\"color\":\"#7fff36\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T22:41:05.529Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-26T22:07:52.791Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true},{\"id\":\"6aa726811239157d744e4274\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"We are all connected\",\"sort_key\":\"We are all connected\",\"description\":\"<p>A reflection on ancestral spirits and our broken bond with Nature, told through compelling imagery and an Inuit perspective.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789858326530temp-1789858326480-cover.jpg\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789858326754temp-1789858326719-poster.jpg\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1789858326268temp-1789858326129-still.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2025\",\"runtime\":\"4\",\"language\":\"Kalaallisut\",\"country\":\"Greenland\",\"subtitle_language\":\"English\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Arina Kleist\",\"screenwriter\":\"Arina Kleist\",\"producer\":\"Arina Kleist, Princess Daazhraii Johnson\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"62eafd839957df004bd01b7b\",\"name\":\"Short\",\"color\":\"#7fff36\",\"visible\":true},{\"id\":\"62eafd6b54339000d369108b\",\"name\":\"microIndigenous\",\"color\":\"#fffc36\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T22:41:05.527Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-19T22:52:06.126Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true}],\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-30T19:43:30.646Z\",\"is_virtual\":false,\"comscore_include\":true,\"geographic_restrictions\":[],\"geographic_exclusions\":[],\"vague_geographic_restrictions\":false,\"show_in_coming_soon\":false,\"allow_preorder\":false,\"aarp_member_required\":false,\"show_quantity_countdown\":false,\"virtual_balloting_enabled\":false,\"virtual_balloting_inline_during_playback\":false,\"use_default_event_bucket_preroll\":true,\"virtual_content_preroll\":[],\"virtual_content_preroll_visible\":true,\"use_default_event_bucket_postroll\":true,\"virtual_content_postroll\":[],\"virtual_content_postroll_visible\":true,\"virtual_intervals\":null,\"display_ads\":[],\"images\":{},\"ledger_tags\":[],\"rules\":[]},{\"id\":\"6aac851fbd583cacc23d147b\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"timezone\":\"Europe/London\",\"name\":\"SPI + Dir. Sayun Simung conversation\",\"description\":\"\",\"short_description\":\"\",\"location\":\"SOAS Centre For Taiwan Studies (SWLT)\",\"venue\":{\"id\":\"6aac856a03b53c4d24cefd8f\",\"name\":\"SOAS Centre For Taiwan Studies (SWLT)\",\"short_name\":\"SOAS CTS\",\"description\":\"\",\"address\":\"SWLT (Wolfson Lecture Theatre), Paul Webley Wing, Senate House, SOAS University of London, \\n10 Thornhaugh Street,\\nRussell Square,\\nLondon\\nWC1H 0XG\",\"default_capacity\":82,\"color\":\"#ffbc57\",\"use_reserved_seating\":false,\"comscore_include\":false},\"is_dated\":true,\"start_time\":\"2026-11-17T17:30:00.000Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-11-17T19:30:00.000Z\",\"cutoff_event_watch_at_availability_end\":false,\"tags\":[],\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"hide_tickets_button\":false,\"require_mailing_address\":false,\"require_phone_number\":false,\"rush_line_enabled\":false,\"passholder_ticket_required\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_enabled\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_unlocked\":false,\"sales_disabled_unless_coupon\":false,\"show_custom_checkout_message\":false,\"external_tickets_url\":\"https://www.soas.ac.uk/about/event/documentary-screening-and-director-qa-spi-2025\",\"disable_pass_quick_order\":false,\"credits_disabled\":true,\"tickets_available\":true,\"unlimited\":false,\"quantity\":0,\"ticket_buckets\":[],\"films\":[{\"id\":\"6aa726811239157d744e4280\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"62a22d5b56023e004d3e6e7c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Native Spirit Festival\",\"owner_id\":\"622b80660c2aa400d1c227ae\",\"name\":\"SPI\",\"sort_key\":\"SPI\",\"short_description\":\"Filmed over the course of ten years, the director documents her own family’s journey with honesty and care—bearing witness to the loss of culture, language, and ceremony.\",\"description\":\"<p><strong>Screening followed by conversation with Director Sayun Simung (online)</strong></p><p><strong>Native Spirit Festival collaboration with SOAS Centre for Taiwan Studies</strong></p><p><br></p><p>This is a story about an Indigenous family living in postcolonial Taiwan.</p><p><br></p><p>After the passing of the grandfather, emotional and cultural rifts between the older and younger generations begin to surface. The grandmother, consumed by grief, clings to the traditional Tayal belief system of Gaga, while the younger members of the family struggle to find their footing in a modern world. Within dreams, ancestral rituals, and the warmth of the firehouse, the family searches for ways to reconnect with their roots and to carry forward the spiritual essence of Gaga in contemporary life.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/83340add9394b6b5ee6edb36ed8563fc.jpg?fit=crop&w=960&h=380\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/97d72a500671d5d9fc8f13b9dc696a5a.jpg?w=300\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1be617a29f5b700b8b208da4f78f08a9.jpg\",\"trailer_url\":\"https://youtu.be/4WfCbrFR47k\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2025\",\"runtime\":\"98\",\"language\":\"Mandarin\",\"country\":\"Taiwan\",\"facebook\":\"https://www.facebook.com/SqoyawFilm\",\"subtitle_language\":\"English\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Sayun Simung\",\"producer\":\"Huang Hui-chen\",\"animator\":null,\"cast\":null,\"cinematographer\":null,\"co_producer\":null,\"composer\":null,\"editor\":\"Lin I-chu\",\"executive_producer\":null,\"filmmaker\":null,\"music\":null,\"production_design\":null,\"screenwriter\":null,\"sound_design\":null},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"635802d3f4bc74007700df78\",\"name\":\"Documentary\",\"color\":\"#ff8fdc\",\"visible\":true}],\"imdb_id\":null,\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-13T22:41:05.539Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-14T13:58:51.475Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true}],\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-28T18:53:26.861Z\",\"is_virtual\":false,\"comscore_include\":true,\"geographic_restrictions\":[],\"geographic_exclusions\":[],\"vague_geographic_restrictions\":false,\"show_in_coming_soon\":false,\"allow_preorder\":false,\"aarp_member_required\":false,\"show_quantity_countdown\":false,\"virtual_balloting_enabled\":false,\"virtual_balloting_inline_during_playback\":false,\"use_default_event_bucket_preroll\":true,\"virtual_content_preroll\":[],\"virtual_content_preroll_visible\":true,\"use_default_event_bucket_postroll\":true,\"virtual_content_postroll\":[],\"virtual_content_postroll_visible\":true,\"virtual_intervals\":null,\"display_ads\":[],\"images\":{},\"ledger_tags\":[],\"rules\":[]}],\"includes_all_events\":false}",
